{\"conversation_id\":\"\",\"created_at\":1791373887,\"error\":null,\"id\":\"resp_20261007194848e6bfe536f20e4886\",\"incomplete_details\":null,\"instructions\":\"You are PIA (Pi-ABAP Agent), written in ABAP, running on the model glm-5.3 (z.ai) through backend OSG-STORE. If asked which model you are, say exactly that; never claim another model or vendor. Tools: read_object(name), write_source(name, source - FULL source, include main|testclasses), activate(name), run_tests(name). Rules: read before write; write full source; always activate after write; if activation says publish pending, finish the turn and run_tests in the next turn. Answer briefly in the user language. Your own code: ZCL_PIA_00_EXECUTOR (agent loop), ZCL_PIA_00_LLM_HTTP (LLM client: builds requests, parses responses and tool calls), ZCL_PIA_00_JSON_UTIL (JSON helpers), ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION and ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION_STORE (conversation), ZCL_PIA_00_REGISTRY (tools), ZCL_PIA_15_T_* (the tools), ZCL_PIA_20_B_* (backends), ZCL_PIA_30_* (terminal, turns). Unit tests live in the testclasses include of a class.\",\"metadata\":null,\"model\":\"glm-5.3\",\"object\":\"response\",\"output\":[{\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Interesting: ZCL_PIA_00_LLM_HTTP has no tests (GREEN with 0 methods). Wait \u2014 but I got 30 methods listed for JSON_UTIL... wait, the first result was labeled \\\"RED tests ran\\\" for JSON_UTIL with LTCL_JSON_UTIL having 30 methods including ESCAPE_EMOJI_PAIR. Hmm, actually in the previous turn the run for JSON_UTIL showed 30 methods? No wait, in this turn: run_tests JSON_UTIL \u2192 30 methods, 29 pass, 1 fail (ESCAPE_EMOJI_PAIR, in testclasses line 413). run_tests LLM_HTTP \u2192 0 classes/methods, no tests.\\n\\nWait, hold on. Actually the first result shown is ZCL_PIA_00_JSON_UTIL? It says target CLAS ZCL_PIA_00_JSON_UTIL, LTCL_JSON_UTIL, 30 methods. Yes.\\n\\nSo LLM_HTTP has no tests \u2192 safe to create testclasses include there with my reproduction test. \\n\\nPlan:\\n1. Write testclasses for ZCL_PIA_00_LLM_HTTP with a test reproducing the bug: parse_calls_responses (and parse_calls_chat) with two tool calls, first arguments containing `lv_open = '{'.`. Assert 2 calls, correct ids/names/arguments. This is red now.\\n2. Also maybe add JSON_UTIL-level tests for split_entries/extract_balanced string-awareness \u2014 but JSON_UTIL testclasses exist and I can't read them, so I can't add there without clobbering. I could add those unit tests in LLM_HTTP's testclasses too (calling zcl_pia_00_json_util methods). That's fine \u2014 tests can call any class.\\n\\nActually, better: put a focused test on split_entries + extract_balanced + parse_calls_responses + parse_calls_chat all in LLM_HTTP testclasses. run_tests(ZCL_PIA_00_LLM_HTTP) runs local tests of that class. Good.\\n\\n3. Fix the code:\\n   - JSON_UTIL split_entries: string-aware.\\n   - JSON_UTIL extract_balanced: string-aware (standard JSON strings, case A).\\n   - LLM_HTTP parse_calls_chat / parse_calls_responses: arguments via extract_str + unescape with fallback to extract_balanced for object-typed arguments.\\n\\nCareful with extract_balanced fix and case A vs case B: extract_balanced with `arguments` key + `{`/`}` \u2014 after fix it remains case-A-aware. If arguments is a string value (case B), the fixed extract_balanced would now behave how? Trace: lv_rest = `\\\"arguments\\\":\\\"{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":...}\\\"...`; first `{` = content open (depth 1). Next char `\\\"` \u2192 in_str = true. Then `\\\\` \u2192 skip `\\\"` (the escaped one). ... continues; content inner quotes are all `\\\\\\\"` \u2192 skipped \u2192 in_str stays true through the whole content \u2192 the content's closing `}` is \\\"in string\\\" \u2192 ignored \u2192 scan continues past the outer `\\\"` (closes string, in_str=false), then `,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}` \u2014 strings toggle, final `}` counts \u2192 depth 0 at entry end. So extract_balanced for a string-valued arguments returns `{content}\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}` \u2014 the OLD buggy overreach. So extract_balanced alone can't fix case B; hence switching arguments extraction to extract_str is REQUIRED. Good that I planned it.\\n\\nBut wait \u2014 there's also `build_input_items` for tool messages: extract_str 'content' on the tool message. Fine already.\\n\\nAlso `parse_calls_chat` entries: chat format entry:\\n`{\\\"id\\\":\\\"call_1\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"function\\\",\\\"function\\\":{\\\"name\\\":\\\"write_source\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":\\\"{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":...}\\\"}}`\\nNote: arguments is nested inside \\\"function\\\". Current code does extract_balanced(lv_e, key='arguments') \u2014 finds `\\\"arguments\\\"` anywhere in entry \u2014 works. With extract_str same. OK.\\n\\nAlso note in chat format the entry itself has nested braces (function object) \u2014 split_entries with naive counting currently handles it since balanced; with string-awareness still fine.\\n\\nEdge: what about `unescape` of arguments containing `\\\\u`? fine.\\n\\nNow let me also think about whether to keep a fallback: if extract_str returns empty (e.g., provider sends arguments as real object `{\\\"name\\\":...}` \u2014 some do), fall back to extract_balanced. I'll implement:\\n\\n```\\nls-arguments = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eunescape( COND #( LET lv_s = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eextract_str( iv_json = lv_e iv_name = 'arguments' ) IN WHEN lv_s IS NOT INITIAL THEN lv_s ELSE zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eextract_balanced( iv_json = lv_e iv_key = 'arguments' iv_open = '{' iv_close = '}' ) ) ).\\n```\\n\\nHmm, COND with LET is okay in OSG/SAP? COND # LET ... IN is standard 7.40+. The codebase uses COND # already. But to be safe and readable, use explicit variables:\\n\\n```\\nDATA(lv_args) = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eextract_str( iv_json = lv_e iv_name = 'arguments' ).\\nIF lv_args IS INITIAL.\\n  lv_args = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eextract_balanced( iv_json = lv_e iv_key = 'arguments' iv_open = '{' iv_close = '}' ).\\nENDIF.\\nls-arguments = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eunescape( lv_args ).\\n```\\n\\nWait \u2014 careful: for object-valued arguments, unescape would mangle nothing much (no escapes present) \u2014 fine.\\n\\nHmm, one more consideration: extract_str uses PCRE. In open-abap / SAP, PCRE available (they already use PCRE in extract_str and session from_json). Long strings with PCRE `((?:[^\\\"\\\\\\\\]|\\\\\\\\.)*)` \u2014 potential performance issue on huge sources (60KB) but acceptable; it's linear.\\n\\nBUT: there's a subtlety with extract_str and FIND FIRST OCCURRENCE OF PCRE: the regex `\\\"arguments\\\"\\\\s*:\\\\s*\\\"...\\\"` \u2014 fine.\\n\\nAnother subtlety: the entry text for chat format contains \\\"arguments\\\" only once; for responses format once. OK.\\n\\nNow also check: does anything else depend on the old overreaching behavior of extract_balanced with arguments? `flatten_tools` \u2014 key 'function', object value (case A) \u2014 fix improves. `build_input_items` \u2014 tool_calls array (case A). `from_json` \u2014 messages array (case A). answer extraction `output` array (case A). All improved by string-awareness.\\n\\nNow \u2014 the split_entries fix. Current signature returns string_table. New implementation:\\n\\n```\\nMETHOD split_entries.\\n  DATA lv_len_arr TYPE i.\\n  lv_len_arr = strlen( iv_arr ).\\n  DATA lv_pos TYPE i VALUE 0.\\n  WHILE lv_pos \\u003c lv_len_arr.\\n    FIND FIRST OCCURRENCE OF '{' IN iv_arr+lv_pos MATCH OFFSET DATA(lv_off).\\n    IF sy-subrc \\u003c\\u003e 0. EXIT. ENDIF.\\n    DATA lv_start TYPE i.\\n    lv_start = lv_pos + lv_off.\\n    IF lv_start \\u003e= lv_len_arr. EXIT. ENDIF.\\n    DATA lv_depth TYPE i VALUE 1.\\n    DATA lv_str TYPE abap_bool VALUE abap_false.\\n    DATA lv_end TYPE i.\\n    lv_end = lv_start.\\n    WHILE lv_end \\u003c lv_len_arr - 1 AND lv_depth \\u003e 0.\\n      lv_end = lv_end + 1.\\n      DATA lv_ch TYPE string.\\n      lv_ch = iv_arr+lv_end(1).\\n      IF lv_str = abap_true.\\n        IF lv_ch = `\\\\`.\\n          lv_end = lv_end + 1.  \\\" skip escaped char\\n        ELSEIF lv_ch = `\\\"`.\\n          lv_str = abap_false.\\n        ENDIF.\\n      ELSE.\\n        IF lv_ch = `\\\"`.\\n          lv_str = abap_true.\\n        ELSEIF lv_ch = '{'.\\n          lv_depth = lv_depth + 1.\\n        ELSEIF lv_ch = '}'.\\n          lv_depth = lv_depth - 1.\\n        ENDIF.\\n      ENDIF.\\n    ENDWHILE.\\n    ...\\n```\\n\\nHmm wait: when depth reaches 0 via `}` we stop \u2014 good. When `\\\\` at position lv_len_arr-1: lv_end incremented beyond; loop condition catches.\\n\\nBut hold on \u2014 the `FIND FIRST OCCURRENCE OF '{'` for entry start: the first `{` in the array \u2014 if there is preceding garbage... fine.\\n\\nThere's a subtlety though: entries that are objects at top level start with `{` outside any string. Since we always resume at lv_end+1 right after a closing `}` at depth 0, we're outside strings. Good.\\n\\nBUT: important interplay \u2014 the arguments string content: when split_entries scans entry 1, at `\\\"arguments\\\"` value: `\\\"` toggles lv_str=true; inside, `\\\\\\\"` skipped; the literal `{` inside source \u2014 we're in_str \u2192 ignored. The content `{` and `}` \u2014 in_str \u2192 ignored. Closing `\\\"` of the arguments value \u2192 lv_str=false. Then `,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}` \u2192 final `}` depth 0. Entry 1 ends exactly at its own `}`. Then entry 2 found. So split_entries works with standard string-awareness even for case B strings \u2014 because the outer quotes are normal `\\\"`. The confusion earlier was only for extract_balanced which starts INSIDE the string. Good.\\n\\nSimilarly extract_balanced for arrays (`output`, `tool_calls`): starts outside strings, standard awareness works.\\n\\nWait, one more check on extract_balanced for `tool_calls` in build_input_items/chat parsing: message content like `{\\\"tool_calls\\\":[{...}]}`... fine.\\n\\nNow, hmm, about extract_balanced starting position: `FIND FIRST OCCURRENCE OF iv_open IN lv_rest` \u2014 iv_open is `{` or `[`. Could the first `{` after the key be inside a string? E.g. `\\\"text\\\":\\\"use { here\\\"` before... the key search positions us at the key; the open search starts from the key. Between key and its value there's `\\\":[` or `\\\":{` or `\\\":\\\"`. If value is a string starting with `{`... e.g. `\\\"arguments\\\":\\\"{\\\"`? Only if arguments content starts with `{` \u2014 that IS the case B which we handle via extract_str now. For case A (array/object values), the first open char after key is the value's opening \u2014 unless the key match landed inside some other string (e.g. the word \\\"output\\\" inside a text). Pre-existing limitation; keep.\\n\\nNow \u2014 while fixing, keep backward compat for existing JSON_UTIL tests: BALANCED_OBJECT, BALANCED_NESTED_AND_ARRAY, BALANCED_MISSING_KEY, BALANCED_NO_OPEN_BRACKET, BALANCED_UNCLOSED must stay green.\\n\\n- BALANCED_UNCLOSED: unclosed \u2192 returns to end (WHILE ends at strlen-1, depth\\u003e0) \u2014 my new loop: same structure, returns lv_rest+lv_start(strlen-1 - lv_start + 1) = to end. Must keep.\\n- BALANCED_NESTED_AND_ARRAY: nested braces/brackets with probably no strings \u2014 works.\\n\\nLet me now also double check the test for extract_balanced unclosed with in_str: if string never closed... loop ends at end. fine.\\n\\nNow write the tests in LLM_HTTP testclasses. Reproduce exactly the reported scenario \u2014 responses API body with two function_call items, first with source containing `lv_open = '{'.`:\\n\\nBody (responses format):\\n```\\n{\\\"id\\\":\\\"resp_1\\\",\\\"output\\\":[\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"function_call\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"fc_1\\\",\\\"call_id\\\":\\\"c1\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"write_source\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":\\\"{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ZCL_PIA_DEMO\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"source\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"CLASS zcl_pia_demo. METHOD run. DATA lv_open TYPE string. lv_open = '{'. ENDMETHOD.\\\\\\\"}\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"},\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"function_call\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"fc_2\\\",\\\"call_id\\\":\\\"c2\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"read_object\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":\\\"{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ZCL_PIA_JSON_UTIL\\\\\\\"}\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}\\n]}\\n```\\n\\nExpected after fix:\\n- 2 calls.\\n- call 1: id c1, name write_source, arguments = `{\\\"name\\\":\\\"ZCL_PIA_DEMO\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"CLASS zcl_pia_demo. METHOD run. DATA lv_open TYPE string. lv_open = '{'. ENDMETHOD.\\\"}`.\\n- call 2: id c2, name read_object, arguments `{\\\"name\\\":\\\"ZCL_PIA_JSON_UTIL\\\"}`.\\n\\nCurrently (red): 1 call with garbage arguments.\\n\\nNote: in ABAP string literals with backslashes: I need to write the JSON with `\\\\\\\"` sequences. In ABAP, backslash isn't an escape in '...' literals (only '' for quote). So `'{\\\"arguments\\\":\\\"{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\"...\\\"}'` is fine as-is in ABAP source: backslash is a normal char in ABAP string literals. \\n\\nBuilding test body: I'll build with string templates |...| \u2014 careful: |...| templates treat { } as embedding? In string templates, `{ ... }` is for embedding expressions! Yes: in | | templates, `{ expr }` embeds. Literal `{` in a template must be escaped how? Actually in string templates, `{` and `}` are only special when forming `{ ... }` around an expression \u2014 the parser looks for matching... hmm. A literal `lv_open = '{'.` inside a | | template: the `{` would start an embedded expression until `}`. `'{'.` \u2014 the embedded expression would be `'{'.`... that would be a syntax error or weird. Safer: use '...' literals (no template interpretation) and concatenate with \\u0026\\u0026. In '...' literals, `{` `}` are plain chars. \\n\\nSo build the body as ABAP single-quoted strings concatenated. Quotes inside: doubled ''. The JSON contains many `\\\"` \u2014 each becomes `\\\"` in ABAP as `\\\"` \u2014 no wait, in ABAP '...' literal, a single quote inside must be doubled: 'it''s'. JSON `\\\"` is a double quote char \u2014 in an ABAP '...' literal, `\\\"` is just a normal character (no escaping needed). Yes! ABAP text literals use ' as delimiter; \\\" inside is fine. And backslash fine. So:\\n\\n```\\nDATA lv_body TYPE string.\\nlv_body = '{\\\"output\\\":[' \\u0026\\u0026\\n          '{\\\"type\\\":\\\"function_call\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"fc_1\\\",\\\"call_id\\\":\\\"c1\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"write_source\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":\\\"{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ZCL_PIA_DEMO\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"source\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"CLASS z. lv_open = ''{''.\\\\\\\"}\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"},' \\u0026\\u0026\\n          ...\\n```\\n\\nCareful: the `'{''` in the ABAP source inside the JSON: the JSON source string content contains `lv_open = '{'.` \u2014 the single quotes are literal `'` chars in JSON. In an ABAP '...' literal each `'` must be doubled: `lv_open = ''{''.` \u2192 represents `lv_open = '{'.`. Good.\\n\\nExpected arguments value (after unescape): `{\\\"name\\\":\\\"ZCL_PIA_DEMO\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"CLASS z. lv_open = '{'.\\\"}`. In ABAP literal: `'{\\\"name\\\":\\\"ZCL_PIA_DEMO\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"CLASS z. lv_open = ''{'''.'}'` \u2014 careful at the end: content ends with `'.` then `\\\"}`. Let me just write expected as concatenation too.\\n\\nAlso chat format test:\\n```\\n{\\\"choices\\\":[{\\\"message\\\":{\\\"tool_calls\\\":[\\n{\\\"id\\\":\\\"c1\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"function\\\",\\\"function\\\":{\\\"name\\\":\\\"write_source\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":\\\"{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ZCL_X\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"source\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"... '{' ...\\\\\\\"}\\\"}},\\n{\\\"id\\\":\\\"c2\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"function\\\",\\\"function\\\":{\\\"name\\\":\\\"read_object\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":\\\"{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ZCL_Y\\\\\\\"}\\\"}}\\n]}}]}\\n```\\nparse_calls_chat on this: extract_balanced(body, 'tool_calls', '[', ']') \u2192 array content; split_entries; per entry extract id/name/arguments. Same bug. I'll test both.\\n\\nAlso add JSON_UTIL-level tests (in the same LLM_HTTP testclasses, or better: keep tests near the fix \u2014 but JSON_UTIL's testclasses can't be preserved... I don't have its content. I could write a second local test class LTCL_JSON_BRACES in LLM_HTTP's testclasses include testing split_entries/extract_balanced directly. That's acceptable.\\n\\nHmm, actually wait \u2014 maybe I should double-check whether testclasses include exists but empty for LLM_HTTP (run said 0 classes). Fine \u2014 writing fresh.\\n\\nAlso I must think about whether write_source with include=testclasses creates the include properly. Yes.\\n\\nTest method list for LTCL_PARSE_CALLS (in LLM_HTTP):\\n1. RESPONSES_BRACE_IN_STRING_TWO_CALLS \u2014 the bug repro.\\n2. CHAT_BRACE_IN_STRING_TWO_CALLS \u2014 chat variant.\\n3. SPLIT_ENTRIES_IGNORES_BRACES_IN_STRINGS (JSON_UTIL direct).\\n4. EXTRACT_BALANCED_IGNORES_BRACES_IN_STRINGS (JSON_UTIL direct) \u2014 e.g. `{\\\"output\\\":[{\\\"text\\\":\\\"a{b\\\"}]}` extract output array... wait extract_balanced with open `[`: scanning must skip `{` inside string. Test: `{\\\"a\\\":\\\"[\\\",\\\"b\\\":[1]}` key 'b' \u2192 should return `[1]` not `[\\\"[\\\",...`. Hmm: naive: finds `[` inside string `\\\"[\\\"` first \u2192 wrong start. With my fix, the open search is still `FIND FIRST iv_open` \u2014 NOT string-aware! `{\\\"a\\\":\\\"[\\\",\\\"b\\\":[1]}` \u2014 FIND first `[` \u2192 the one inside string. So extract_balanced would start there: then `\\\",\\\"b\\\":[1]}` scanning... depth counting string-aware: after `[` (start), `\\\"` opens str... `\\\"` closes... `,` `\\\"` ... hmm result `[\\\",\\\"b\\\":[1]}`? Let me not include that pathological case; the FIND for open isn't fixed. Should I fix the open-search too? For key 'b': to be correct we'd need string-aware search for the opening char. Doable: scan from key position, tracking in_str, find first iv_open outside string. Let me implement that properly \u2014 it's easy and more correct:\\n\\n```\\n\\\" find first opening char outside a string\\nDATA lv_i TYPE i.\\nlv_i = 0. \\\" relative in lv_rest... \\n```\\n\\nHmm wait, but careful with case B again: for arguments (string value), lv_rest starts at `\\\"arguments\\\"` and the first `{` outside a string \u2014 the outer `\\\"` right after colon opens a string \u2192 in_str until the closing `\\\"` \u2014 the content `{` would be \\\"inside string\\\" \u2192 not found! Then we'd return empty for arguments. But we're switching arguments to extract_str anyway, and fallback only when extract_str is empty (object value \u2192 not string \u2192 works). Hmm, but if someone calls extract_balanced directly with a string-valued key... old code \\\"worked\\\" by luck. My LLM_HTTP test for extract_balanced will use array/object cases only.\\n\\nActually wait \u2014 careful about the start-search string-awareness and the KEY position itself: FIND `\\\"key\\\"` in iv_json might land inside a string too. Not fixing that (pre-existing).\\n\\nHmm, actually, should I make the open-char search string-aware? It adds robustness for arrays whose preceding sibling fields contain `[`/`{` in strings \u2014 e.g. `output` array: FIND '\\\"output\\\"' \u2192 ok, then first `[` after it \u2014 the value's `[` typically immediately follows. A preceding field with `[` in a string AFTER the key \\\"output\\\"? Can't be \u2014 the key is immediately before its value. Between key and value only `:` and whitespace. So the first open char after the key is the value's open \u2014 UNLESS the value is a string (case B) or the value is a scalar and the open char found belongs to a LATER field (e.g. key missing/not an object). E.g. `{\\\"text\\\":\\\"x\\\",\\\"list\\\":[1]}` searching key 'text' open '[': first `[` after \\\"text\\\" is the list's. Pre-existing semantic; whatever.\\n\\nOK: keep FIND for open char (minimal change), but make the depth scan string-aware. That fixes the reported bug combined with extract_str for arguments.\\n\\nHmm, wait \u2014 actually let me reconsider making the open-search string-aware: for `parse_calls_responses`, the body: `{\\\"output\\\":[...]}` \u2014 FIND '\\\"output\\\"' \u2192 first occurrence could be... the body starts `{\\\"id\\\":...,\\\"output\\\":[...]}`. Fine.\\n\\nAlright, let me also reconsider: do I even need extract_balanced changes for the bug? The reported repro: two calls. The failures were (a) split_entries merging entries (second lost) and (b) arguments overreach. (a) fixed by split_entries string-awareness. (b) fixed by extract_str for arguments. extract_balanced string-awareness is a bonus robustness fix (e.g. text containing brackets inside the output array before... hmm, actually for the `output` array extraction: body `{\\\"output\\\":[{...,\\\"arguments\\\":\\\"...\\\"}]}` \u2014 depth counting of `[`/`]`: strings containing `[` or `]`? ABAP sources rarely contain `[`... they do: `VALUE #( )`? no brackets. `lt[ 1 ]` line expressions! Yes ABAP has `DATA(lv) = lt[ 1 ]-val.` \u2014 brackets inside source strings \u2192 could break `output` array extraction. So worth fixing.)\\n\\nBut careful: fixing extract_balanced depth scan for case B (arguments) changes its behavior from \\\"overreach\\\" to \\\"overreach further\\\"? Let me re-trace with string-aware scan for arguments case B: start at content `{` depth 1; next char `\\\"` \u2192 in_str=true; all inner `\\\\\\\"` skipped; outer closing `\\\"` \u2192 in_str=false; then `,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}` \u2192 `}` depth 0 \u2192 returns `{content}\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}` \u2014 same as before (old code returned exactly this too, since the literal `{` bumped depth and the entry's closing `}` closed it). Same overreach \u2014 fine, because we no longer use it for arguments (except fallback when extract_str empty, i.e. object value \u2192 case A \u2192 correct).\\n\\nNow let me also double check `parse_calls_chat` entry structure for extract_str 'id': entry `{\\\"id\\\":\\\"c1\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"function\\\",\\\"function\\\":{\\\"name\\\":\\\"write_source\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":\\\"...\\\"}}` \u2014 extract_str 'id' \u2192 `c1`. name \u2192 `write_source`. arguments \u2192 the escaped content. Good. But note: chat entry contains `\\\"function\\\":{\\\"name\\\":...}` \u2014 if the tool name were \\\"id\\\"... irrelevant.\\n\\nOne more: in parse_calls_responses, filter `IF lv_e NS '\\\"function_call\\\"' AND lv_e NS '\\\"type\\\":\\\"function_call\\\"'. CONTINUE.` \u2014 entry 1 merged previously contained both; after fix each entry contains `\\\"type\\\":\\\"function_call\\\"`. Good.\\n\\nNow, also the executor: no changes needed \u2014 bug is purely parsing. But wait, the user said \\\"PIA runs only the first call\\\" \u2014 after fix both calls run. Also verify build_input_items round-trip with `'{''` in stored arguments: assistant raw message `{\\\"tool_calls\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"c1\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"write_source\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":\\\"escaped\\\"}]}` where escaped = escape(arguments) \u2014 escape turns `'` fine, `{` fine (not escaped, stays literal `{`), `\\\"` \u2192 `\\\\\\\"`. Then build_input_items: extract_str 'arguments' \u2192 returns escaped content, embedded into `\\\"arguments\\\":\\\"...\\\"`. Then next request JSON valid. \\n\\nAlso `ev_assistant_raw` and session storage fine.\\n\\nNow \u2014 is there any place that parses the assistant raw message back with brace counting? build_input_items uses extract_str for arguments. Good.\\n\\nLet me now write the testclasses include for ZCL_PIA_00_LLM_HTTP.\\n\\nTest class LTCL_PARSE_CALLS with FOR TESTING methods. Also LTCL_JSON_BRACES for JSON_UTIL. Since JSON_UTIL already has its own local test class in its own include, having another local class in LLM_HTTP testing JSON_UTIL methods is fine (different compilation unit, global class access is fine).\\n\\nWrite the tests FIRST (red), run to confirm red, then fix, then run again (green). But note: run_tests runs on PUBLISHED active code \u2014 after writing testclasses I must ACTIVATE the class, then run tests. The activate tool publishes; \\\"the new code becomes live in the NEXT step\\\". So sequence: write testclasses \u2192 activate \u2192 run_tests (red expected for new tests) \u2192 write fixed main includes (JSON_UTIL + LLM_HTTP) \u2192 activate both \u2192 run_tests both (green except ESCAPE_EMOJI_PAIR red in JSON_UTIL).\\n\\nCareful: when I write LLM_HTTP main include later, I must rewrite the FULL source with my modifications. Same for JSON_UTIL. Both were read \u2014 good.\\n\\nLet me now compose the test include.\\n\\n```abap\\nCLASS ltcl_parse_calls DEFINITION FINAL FOR TESTING\\n  DURATION SHORT RISK LEVEL HARMLESS.\\n\\n  PRIVATE SECTION.\\n    METHODS responses_two_calls_brace_in_string FOR TESTING.\\n    METHODS chat_two_calls_brace_in_string FOR TESTING.\\n    METHODS split_entries_ignores_braces_in_strings FOR TESTING.\\n    METHODS extract_balanced_ignores_braces_in_strings FOR TESTING.\\nENDCLASS.\\n\\nCLASS ltcl_parse_calls IMPLEMENTATION.\\n\\n  METHOD responses_two_calls_brace_in_string.\\n    \\\" bug: a single '{' inside the arguments string of the first of two\\n  \\\" function_call items made split_entries swallow the second item and let the\\n    \\\" arguments scan run past the JSON (\\\"...\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"} in the args)\\n    DATA lv_body TYPE string.\\n    lv_body =\\n      '{\\\"id\\\":\\\"resp_1\\\",\\\"output\\\":[' \\u0026\\u0026\\n      '{\\\"type\\\":\\\"function_call\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"fc_1\\\",\\\"call_id\\\":\\\"c1\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"write_source\\\",' \\u0026\\u0026\\n      '\\\"arguments\\\":\\\"{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ZCL_PIA_DEMO\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"source\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"CLASS z. METHOD m. DATA lv_open TYPE string. lv_open = ''{''. ENDMETHOD.\\\\\\\"}\\\",' \\u0026\\u0026\\n      '\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"},' \\u0026\\u0026\\n      '{\\\"type\\\":\\\"function_call\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"fc_2\\\",\\\"call_id\\\":\\\"c2\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"read_object\\\",' \\u0026\\u0026\\n      '\\\"arguments\\\":\\\"{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ZCL_PIA_JSON_UTIL\\\\\\\"}\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}' \\u0026\\u0026\\n      ']}'.\\n\\n    DATA(lt_calls) = zcl_pia_00_llm_http=\\u003eparse_calls_responses( lv_body ).\\n\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals( exp = 2 act = lines( lt_calls ) msg = 'both calls must be parsed' ).\\n\\n    READ TABLE lt_calls INDEX 1 INTO DATA(ls_first).\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals( exp = 'c1' act = ls_first-id ).\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals( exp = 'write_source' act = ls_first-name ).\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\n      exp = '{\\\"name\\\":\\\"ZCL_PIA_DEMO\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"CLASS z. METHOD m. DATA lv_open TYPE string. lv_open = ''{''. ENDMETHOD.\\\"}'\\n      act = ls_first-arguments\\n      msg = 'arguments must end at the JSON end, no trailing status/call_id' ).\\n\\n    READ TABLE lt_calls INDEX 2 INTO DATA(ls_second).\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals( exp = 'c2' act = ls_second-id ).\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals( exp = 'read_object' act = ls_second-name ).\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals( exp = '{\\\"name\\\":\\\"ZCL_PIA_JSON_UTIL\\\"}' act = ls_second-arguments ).\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\n  ...\\n```\\n\\nWait: expected arguments after unescape: unescape turns `\\\\\\\"` \u2192 `\\\"`. Source in JSON: `\\\\\\\"source\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"CLASS z. ... lv_open = ''{''. ENDMETHOD.\\\\\\\"` \u2014 unescaped \u2192 `\\\"source\\\":\\\"CLASS z. ... lv_open = '{'. ENDMETHOD.\\\"`. Full: `{\\\"name\\\":\\\"ZCL_PIA_DEMO\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"CLASS z. METHOD m. DATA lv_open TYPE string. lv_open = '{'. ENDMETHOD.\\\"}`. In ABAP literal: the `'{'.` part \u2192 `''{''.`. And the whole literal in '...': no double quotes to escape (they're plain), single quotes doubled. End: `... ENDMETHOD.\\\"}'` \u2192 `... ENDMETHOD.\\\"}` then closing ABAP quote. OK.\\n\\nNote the tt_calls type: zif_pia_00_tool=\\u003ett_calls \u2014 table of ts_call with id, name, arguments... let me confirm field names: ts_call has id, name, arguments (from parse code: ls-id, ls-name, ls-arguments). And registry used is_call-name, is_call-arguments, is_call-id. Good.\\n\\nChat test:\\n\\n```abap\\n  METHOD chat_two_calls_brace_in_string.\\n    DATA lv_body TYPE string.\\n    lv_body =\\n      '{\\\"id\\\":\\\"chat_1\\\",\\\"choices\\\":[{\\\"index\\\":0,\\\"message\\\":{' \\u0026\\u0026\\n      '\\\"role\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"content\\\":null,\\\"tool_calls\\\":[' \\u0026\\u0026\\n      '{\\\"id\\\":\\\"c1\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"function\\\",\\\"function\\\":{\\\"name\\\":\\\"write_source\\\",' \\u0026\\u0026\\n      '\\\"arguments\\\":\\\"{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ZCL_X\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"source\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"m1. lv_open = ''{''.\\\\\\\"}\\\"}},' \\u0026\\u0026\\n      '{\\\"id\\\":\\\"c2\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"function\\\",\\\"function\\\":{\\\"name\\\":\\\"read_object\\\",' \\u0026\\u0026\\n      '\\\"arguments\\\":\\\"{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ZCL_Y\\\\\\\"}\\\"}}' \\u0026\\u0026\\n      ']}}]}',\\n```\\n\\nHmm \u2014 careful with JSON validity: each tool_call object: `{\\\"id\\\":\\\"c1\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"function\\\",\\\"function\\\":{...}}`. So first: `{\\\"id\\\":\\\"c1\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"function\\\",\\\"function\\\":{\\\"name\\\":\\\"write_source\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":\\\"...\\\"}}` then comma, then second `{\\\"id\\\":\\\"c2\\\",...}}`. Array closes `]`, then message `}`, choice `}`, choices `]`, root `}`.\\n\\nLet me write:\\n```\\n'{\\\"id\\\":\\\"chat_1\\\",\\\"object\\\":\\\"chat.completion\\\",\\\"choices\\\":[{\\\"index\\\":0,\\\"message\\\":{\\\"role\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"content\\\":null,\\\"tool_calls\\\":[' \\u0026\\u0026\\n'{\\\"id\\\":\\\"c1\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"function\\\",\\\"function\\\":{\\\"name\\\":\\\"write_source\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":\\\"{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ZCL_X\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"source\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"m1. lv_open = ''{''.\\\\\\\"}\\\"}},' \\u0026\\u0026\\n'{\\\"id\\\":\\\"c2\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"function\\\",\\\"function\\\":{\\\"name\\\":\\\"read_object\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":\\\"{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ZCL_Y\\\\\\\"}\\\"}}' \\u0026\\u0026\\n']}}]}'\\n```\\nCheck braces: choice1: { id, type, function:{ name, arguments } } \u2192 `\\\"arguments\\\":\\\"...\\\\\\\"}\\\"` closes function obj, then `}` closes the tool_call, then `,`. In my line: `...\\\\\\\"}\\\"}},` \u2014 that's: `\\\\\\\"` `}` (closes... wait the arguments string content ends with `\\\\\\\"}` \u2014 content = `{\\\"name\\\":\\\"ZCL_X\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"m1. lv_open = '{'.\\\"}` hmm my content is `{\\\"name\\\":\\\"ZCL_X\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"m1. lv_open = '{'.\\\"}`. Encoded: `{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ZCL_X\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"source\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"m1. lv_open = ''{''.\\\\\\\"}` (ABAP doubling for '). Then close the arguments STRING with `\\\"`, then `}` closes function, then `}` closes the tool_call entry, then `,`. So: `'{\\\"id\\\":\\\"c1\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"function\\\",\\\"function\\\":{\\\"name\\\":\\\"write_source\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":\\\"{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ZCL_X\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"source\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"m1. lv_open = ''{''.\\\\\\\"}\\\"}},'`. Count at end: `\\\\\\\"` (escaped quote in content) `}` (content close, inside string) `\\\"` (close arguments string) `}` (close function) `}` (close entry) `,`. So the tail is `...\\\\\\\"}\\\"}},`. In ABAP: `...\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\"}},'`? no \u2014 backslash isn't escaped in ABAP. The literal ends with `\\\"}},` then ABAP quote: `...''{''.\\\\\\\"}\\\"}},'`. Good.\\n\\nEntry2: `{\\\"id\\\":\\\"c2\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"function\\\",\\\"function\\\":{\\\"name\\\":\\\"read_object\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":\\\"{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ZCL_Y\\\\\\\"}\\\"}}` \u2192 tail: `\\\\\\\"}` (content) `\\\"` (close string) `}` (function) `}` (entry). Then `]}}]}` : `]` closes tool_calls, `}` closes message, `}` closes choice, `]` closes choices, `}` root. Wait I wrote `']}}]}'` \u2014 that's `]`,`}`,`}`,`]`,`}` \u2014 but I need `]` tool_calls, `}` message, `}` choice... hold on: choices array contains choice objects; after the second entry there should be `]` (tool_calls) `}` (message) `}` (choice) `]` (choices) `}` (root) \u2192 `]}}]}`. Yes matches.\\n\\nHmm wait, also entry1 within: after `,` comes entry2. But note in my construction the entries are concatenated with `,` \u2014 I have `'...' },' \\u0026\\u0026 '{\\\"id\\\":\\\"c2\\\"...`. Good.\\n\\nExpected parse: 2 calls; first name write_source, arguments `{\\\"name\\\":\\\"ZCL_X\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"m1. lv_open = '{'.\\\"}`; second read_object `{\\\"name\\\":\\\"ZCL_Y\\\"}`.\\n\\nHmm wait \u2014 unescape of `{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ZCL_X\\\\\\\",...\\\\\\\"}` \u2192 `{\\\"name\\\":\\\"ZCL_X\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"m1. lv_open = '{'.\\\"}`. Good.\\n\\nNote: chat parsing extracts 'id' via extract_str \u2014 but entry contains `\\\"id\\\":\\\"c1\\\"` once... also `\\\"index\\\":0` outside. fine. Name: extract_str 'name' \u2192 first \\\"name\\\" in entry = the function name. Good. BUT: extract_str for 'arguments': entry text contains `\\\"arguments\\\":\\\"{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\"...\\\"` \u2014 PCRE `((?:[^\\\"\\\\\\\\]|\\\\\\\\.)*)` \u2014 good.\\n\\nJSON_UTIL direct tests:\\n\\n```abap\\n  METHOD split_entries_ignores_braces_in_strings.\\n    DATA lv_arr TYPE string.\\n    lv_arr = '[{\\\"a\\\":\\\"x{y\\\",\\\"b\\\":1},{\\\"c\\\":\\\"}\\\",\\\"d\\\":2}]'.\\n    DATA(lt) = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003esplit_entries( lv_arr ).\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals( exp = 2 act = lines( lt ) ).\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals( exp = '{\\\"a\\\":\\\"x{y\\\",\\\"b\\\":1}' act = lt[ 1 ] ).\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals( exp = '{\\\"c\\\":\\\"}\\\",\\\"d\\\":2}' act = lt[ 2 ] ).\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\n```\\n\\nCheck with current buggy code: entry1 `{` d1; `\\\"` str... old code has no str: `{`(1) ... `x{y` \u2192 `{` d2; `}` after \\\"c\\\":\\\" \u2192 wait `}` in `\\\"c\\\":\\\"}\\\"` \u2192 d1; `}` end of entry2 \u2192 d0 \u2192 single entry `{\\\"a\\\":\\\"x{y\\\",\\\"b\\\":1},{\\\"c\\\":\\\"}\\\",\\\"d\\\":2}` hmm also `,\\\"b\\\":1}` closes entry1 `}` \u2192 d1; then entry2 `{` \u2192 d2; `\\\"c\\\":\\\"}\\\"` `}` \u2192 d1; end of string with d1 \u2192 lv_end = len-1. One entry. So red now. With fix: 2 entries.\\n\\n```abap\\n  METHOD extract_balanced_ignores_braces_in_strings.\\n    DATA lv_json TYPE string.\\n    lv_json = '{\\\"text\\\":\\\"a]b\\\",\\\"items\\\":[\\\"x\\\"]}';  hmm this tests '[' skip inside string\\n    DATA(lv_arr) = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eextract_balanced(\\n      iv_json = lv_json iv_key = 'items' iv_open = '[' iv_close = ']' ).\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals( exp = '[\\\"x\\\"]' act = lv_arr ).\\n```\\nWith buggy code: FIND '\\\"items\\\"' \u2192 offset; first `[` after \u2192 the `[` inside `\\\"a]b\\\"`? that's a `]` not `[`. Text `a]b` contains `]`. First `[` is items' `[`. depth 1; scan: `\\\"`? wait lv_rest from `\\\"items\\\"`: `\\\"items\\\":[\\\"x\\\"]}`. chars: `[`(start) `\\\"` x `\\\"` `]` \u2192 d0 \u2192 returns `[\\\"x\\\"]`. Hmm \u2014 passes even with bug. Need a case where a `[` appears inside a string BEFORE the real close `]`, or `]`... Let me craft: `{\\\"pre\\\":\\\"[ok]\\\",\\\"items\\\":[\\\"x\\\"]}`: buggy: first `[` after '\\\"items\\\"'? FIND happens from lv_off (key match) \u2014 first `[` in `\\\"items\\\":[\\\"x\\\"]}` is the real one. Hmm the pre field is BEFORE the key. The scan only sees text after the key. So to break it, the `[` must be after key: key 'items' value `[\\\"a[b]c\\\"]`: `{\\\"items\\\":[\\\"a[b]c\\\"]}`: buggy: `[` start d1; `\\\"`a`[` d2; `b` `]` d1; `c` `\\\"` `]` d0 \u2192 returns `[\\\"a[b]c` + ... let me count precisely: chars `[ \\\" a [ b ] c \\\" ]`. start at 0 `[` d1. pos1 `\\\"` pos2 `a` pos3 `[` d2 pos4 `b` pos5 `]` d1 pos6 `c` pos7 `\\\"` pos8 `]` d0 \u2192 extracted `[\\\"a[b]c\\\"]` \u2014 actually complete! Because both `[` and `]` inside. Need UNBALANCED inside string: `[\\\"a[b\\\"]`: chars `[ \\\" a [ b \\\" ]` \u2192 pos3 `[` d2, pos6 `]` d1... never 0 until end \u2192 overreach to end. So test: `{\\\"items\\\":[\\\"a[b\\\"]}` expect `[\\\"a[b\\\"]`. Buggy returns `[\\\"a[b\\\"]}` (to end, including root `}`). With fix: `[\\\"a[b\\\"]`. \\n\\nAlso braces variant: `{\\\"obj\\\":{\\\"s\\\":\\\"a{b\\\"}}` key 'obj' open '{': chars after key: `{ \\\" s \\\" : \\\" a { b \\\" \\\" } }` wait: `{\\\"obj\\\":{\\\"s\\\":\\\"a{b\\\"}}`. lv_rest = `\\\"obj\\\":{\\\"s\\\":\\\"a{b\\\"}}`. `{` start d1; `\\\"`s`\\\"`; `:`; `\\\"`a` `{` d2; `b`; `\\\"`; `}` d1; `}` d0 \u2192 extracted `{\\\"s\\\":\\\"a{b\\\"}` wait \u2014 pos: `{`(d1) `\\\"` `s` `\\\"` `:` `\\\"` `a` `{`(d2) `b` `\\\"` `}`(d1) `}`(d0) \u2192 returns `{\\\"s\\\":\\\"a{b\\\"}`? The full object is `{\\\"s\\\":\\\"a{b\\\"}` \u2014 hold on the actual object `{\\\"s\\\":\\\"a{b\\\"}` \u2014 yes that IS the value; the outer `}}` closes obj and root. Buggy extraction: depth hits 0 at the SECOND `}` (root's), so returns `{\\\"s\\\":\\\"a{b\\\"}}` \u2014 including root `}`. Overreach. With fix: string-aware: `{` d1, `\\\"s\\\"` string, `:` , `\\\"a{b\\\"` string ({ ignored), `}` d0 \u2192 `{\\\"s\\\":\\\"a{b\\\"}`. \\n\\nI'll assert `{\\\"s\\\":\\\"a{b\\\"}`.\\n\\nHmm \u2014 but careful: my planned fix for extract_balanced: does the depth scan start counting from lv_start where in_str=false \u2014 yes at the value's opening brace, outside strings. Good.\\n\\nNow write the LLM_HTTP main-include fix (full source) and JSON_UTIL main fix (full source).\\n\\nJSON_UTIL split_entries new code \u2014 also keep the defensive clamps. Let me write:\\n\\n```abap\\n  METHOD split_entries.\\n    \\\" top-level {...} entries of a JSON array string; braces inside double-quoted\\n    \\\" string values do not count (a lone '{' in ABAP source like lv_open = '{'.\\n    \\\" used to swallow the next entry); every access is clamped\\n    DATA lv_len_arr TYPE i.\\n    lv_len_arr = strlen( iv_arr ).\\n    DATA lv_pos TYPE i VALUE 0.\\n    WHILE lv_pos \\u003c lv_len_arr.\\n      FIND FIRST OCCURRENCE OF '{' IN iv_arr+lv_pos MATCH OFFSET DATA(lv_off).\\n      IF sy-subrc \\u003c\\u003e 0. EXIT. ENDIF.\\n      DATA lv_start TYPE i.\\n      lv_start = lv_pos + lv_off.\\n      IF lv_start \\u003e= lv_len_arr. EXIT. ENDIF.\\n      DATA lv_depth TYPE i.\\n      lv_depth = 1.\\n      DATA lv_in_str TYPE abap_bool.\\n      lv_in_str = abap_false.\\n      DATA lv_end TYPE i.\\n      lv_end = lv_start.\\n      WHILE lv_end \\u003c lv_len_arr - 1 AND lv_depth \\u003e 0.\\n        lv_end = lv_end + 1.\\n        DATA lv_ch TYPE string.\\n        lv_ch = iv_arr+lv_end(1).\\n        IF lv_in_str = abap_true.\\n          IF lv_ch = `\\\\`.\\n            lv_end = lv_end + 1.          \\\" skip the escaped character\\n          ELSEIF lv_ch = `\\\"`.\\n            lv_in_str = abap_false.\\n          ENDIF.\\n        ELSE.\\n          IF lv_ch = `\\\"`.\\n            lv_in_str = abap_true.\\n          ELSEIF lv_ch = '{'.\\n            lv_depth = lv_depth + 1.\\n          ELSEIF lv_ch = '}'.\\n            lv_depth = lv_depth - 1.\\n          ENDIF.\\n        ENDIF.\\n      ENDWHILE.\\n      IF lv_depth \\u003e 0.\\n        lv_end = lv_len_arr - 1.\\n      ENDIF.\\n      ... (rest unchanged)\\n```\\n\\nWait, one problem: `DATA lv_ch` inside loop \u2014 fine in ABAP (declared once). Note: when `\\\\` at last position: lv_end+1 could exceed lv_len_arr-1 \u2192 next WHILE iteration checks lv_end \\u003c lv_len_arr-1 \u2192 exits. But then `iv_arr+lv_end(1)` not accessed. OK.\\n\\nEdge: after `\\\\` skip, could skip past a `}` \u2014 correct per JSON.\\n\\nextract_balanced new scan similarly:\\n\\n```abap\\n  METHOD extract_balanced.\\n    DATA lv_off TYPE i.\\n    DATA(lv_pat) = '\\\"' \\u0026\\u0026 iv_key \\u0026\\u0026 '\\\"'.\\n    FIND lv_pat IN iv_json MATCH OFFSET lv_off.\\n    IF sy-subrc \\u003c\\u003e 0. RETURN. ENDIF.\\n    DATA lv_rest TYPE string.\\n    lv_rest = iv_json+lv_off.\\n    DATA lv_start TYPE i.\\n    FIND FIRST OCCURRENCE OF iv_open IN lv_rest MATCH OFFSET lv_start.\\n    IF sy-subrc \\u003c\\u003e 0. RETURN. ENDIF.\\n    DATA lv_len TYPE i.\\n    lv_len = strlen( lv_rest ).\\n    DATA lv_depth TYPE i.\\n    lv_depth = 1.\\n    DATA lv_in_str TYPE abap_bool.\\n    lv_in_str = abap_false.\\n    DATA lv_pos TYPE i.\\n    lv_pos = lv_start.\\n    WHILE lv_pos \\u003c lv_len - 1 AND lv_depth \\u003e 0.\\n      lv_pos = lv_pos + 1.\\n      DATA lv_ch TYPE string.\\n      lv_ch = lv_rest+lv_pos(1).\\n      IF lv_in_str = abap_true.\\n        IF lv_ch = `\\\\`.\\n          lv_pos = lv_pos + 1.\\n        ELSEIF lv_ch = `\\\"`.\\n          lv_in_str = abap_false.\\n        ENDIF.\\n      ELSE.\\n        IF lv_ch = `\\\"`.\\n          lv_in_str = abap_true.\\n        ELSEIF lv_ch = iv_open.\\n          lv_depth = lv_depth + 1.\\n        ELSEIF lv_ch = iv_close.\\n          lv_depth = lv_depth - 1.\\n        ENDIF.\\n      ENDIF.\\n    ENDWHILE.\\n    DATA(lv_len2) = lv_pos - lv_start + 1.\\n    rv_ = lv_rest+lv_start(lv_len2).\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\n```\\n\\nCareful: original had comment about VALUE with constant. Keep structure. Also `strlen( lv_rest )` computed each iteration originally; I hoist. lv_pos+1 for `\\\\` skip: if that lands at last char... loop cond handles.\\n\\nHmm: one subtle regression risk \u2014 `BALANCED_UNCLOSED` test expects old behavior \\\"returns to end\\\" \u2014 preserved.\\n\\nBut careful about case where iv_open is `[` and a `{` appears \u2014 irrelevant.\\n\\nAnother subtlety: escaped BACKSLASH inside string: `\\\"a\\\\\\\\\\\"` then `\\\"` \u2014 chars `\\\\` skip next (`\\\\`), then `\\\"` closes. Correct.\\n\\nNow LLM_HTTP parse methods:\\n\\n```abap\\n  METHOD parse_calls_chat.\\n    DATA(lv_arr) = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eextract_balanced(\\n      iv_json = iv_body iv_key = 'tool_calls' iv_open = '[' iv_close = ']' ).\\n    LOOP AT zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003esplit_entries( lv_arr ) INTO DATA(lv_e).\\n      DATA ls TYPE zif_pia_00_tool=\\u003ets_call.\\n      ls-id = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eextract_str( iv_json = lv_e iv_name = 'id' ).\\n      ls-name = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eextract_str( iv_json = lv_e iv_name = 'name' ).\\n      ls-arguments = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eunescape( extract_arguments( lv_e ) ).\\n      IF ls-name IS NOT INITIAL.\\n        APPEND ls TO rt_.\\n      ENDIF.\\n    ENDLOOP.\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\n```\\n\\nwith a private class method:\\n\\n```abap\\n  CLASS-METHODS extract_arguments\\n    IMPORTING iv_entry     TYPE string\\n    RETURNING VALUE(rv_)   TYPE string.\\n```\\n\\nimpl:\\n```abap\\n  METHOD extract_arguments.\\n    \\\" arguments arrive as a JSON string (\\\"{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":...}\\\"): take the string value\\n    \\\" (escape-aware) instead of brace counting, which a lone '{' inside the source\\n    \\\" (lv_open = '{'.) used to break; object-valued arguments fall back to braces\\n    rv_ = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eextract_str( iv_json = iv_entry iv_name = 'arguments' ).\\n    IF rv_ IS INITIAL.\\n      rv_ = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eextract_balanced(\\n        iv_json = iv_entry iv_key = 'arguments' iv_open = '{' iv_close = '}' ).\\n    ENDIF.\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\n```\\n\\nparse_calls_responses same replacement.\\n\\nNow, ordering per instructions: write test first, activate, run (red), then fix, activate, run (green). Also must not touch ESCAPE_EMOJI_PAIR (JSON_UTIL testclasses untouched \u2014 I only write MAIN include of JSON_UTIL; testclasses include separate \u2014 good, writing main doesn't clobber testclasses).\\n\\nWait \u2014 does write_source include=main overwrite only main? Yes: \\\"Write the FULL new source of a class include: main (default) or testclasses.\\\"\\n\\nOne risk: writing testclasses for LLM_HTTP \u2014 none exist, fine.\\n\\nLet me write the testclasses now.\\n\\nAlso add a test that the arguments contain no `status`/`call_id` trailing junk \u2014 covered by exact equality assert.\\n\\nOne more consideration on unescape: arguments contain `\\\\n` (escaped newlines in real payloads) \u2014 unescape converts to real newlines; existing behavior kept.\\n\\nAlso: in the responses test body I should make it realistic with `\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"` \u2014 yes included.\\n\\nLet me also double check `parse_calls_responses` filter: `IF lv_e NS '\\\"function_call\\\"' AND lv_e NS '\\\"type\\\":\\\"function_call\\\"'. CONTINUE.` \u2014 `\\\"type\\\":\\\"function_call\\\"` present. Good.\\n\\nNow about assert messages: use cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals( exp = ... act = ... msg = ... ).\\n\\nLet me write the include now. Keep it small and focused.\\n\\nAlso note: ltcl_parse_calls naming; add `FINAL FOR TESTING DURATION SHORT RISK LEVEL HARMLESS`.\\n\\nAfter writing: activate ZCL_PIA_00_LLM_HTTP, then run_tests \u2014 but activation becomes live next step; run_tests note: \\\"If the last activation is not published yet, finish your turn and run tests in the next turn.\\\" The activate result will tell. I'll follow: write testclasses \u2192 activate \u2192 (if pending, end turn) \u2192 run tests (expect red on my 4 new tests) \u2192 write fixes \u2192 activate both \u2192 run tests both.\\n\\nActually to save turns: write testclasses include AND (in same block? no \u2014 write_source for same class twice? I need testclasses first, and main fix later after red run. Different includes of same class \u2014 two write_source calls, could be parallel but then red demonstration is lost. Keep sequential.)\\n\\nLet me write the test include.\",\"type\":\"reasoning_text\"}],\"encrypted_content\":null,\"id\":\"rs_20261007194848e6bfe536f20e4886\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":[],\"type\":\"reasoning\"},{\"content\":[{\"annotations\":[],\"text\":\"No existing tests in ZCL_PIA_00_LLM_HTTP, and ESCAPE_EMOJI_PAIR (red, known) lives in ZCL_PIA_00_JSON_UTIL's testclasses \u2014 I will not touch that include. I have found the cause:\\n\\n**Cause:** `zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003esplit_entries` and `extract_balanced` count `{`/`}` (and `[`/`]`) without being aware of JSON strings. A lone `{` inside the `arguments` string (e.g. from `lv_open = '{'.`) bumps the depth, so `split_entries` swallows the second `function_call` entry into the first (second call lost), and the `arguments` brace scan runs past the JSON end, appending `\\\",\\\"call_id\\\":\\\"c1\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}` to the arguments.\\n\\nStep 1: write the red tests (new testclasses include of ZCL_PIA_00_LLM_HTTP).\",\"type\":\"output_text\"}],\"id\":\"msg_20261007194848e6bfe536f20e4886\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"message\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"include\\\":\\\"testclasses\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"ZCL_PIA_00_LLM_HTTP\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"\\\\\\\" bug reproduction: a single opening brace inside the arguments string of the\\\\n\\\\\\\" first of two tool calls (e.g. ABAP source with lv_open = '{'.) broke the\\\\n\\\\\\\" string-unaware brace counting of split_entries/extract_balanced: the second\\\\n\\\\\\\" call was swallowed and the first arguments ran past the JSON end\\\\nCLASS ltcl_parse_calls DEFINITION FINAL FOR TESTING\\\\n  DURATION SHORT RISK LEVEL HARMLESS.\\\\n\\\\n  PRIVATE SECTION.\\\\n    METHODS responses_two_calls_brace_in_src FOR TESTING.\\\\n    METHODS chat_two_calls_brace_in_src FOR TESTING.\\\\n    METHODS split_entries_skips_strings FOR TESTING.\\\\n    METHODS balanced_skips_strings FOR TESTING.\\\\nENDCLASS.\\\\n\\\\nCLASS ltcl_parse_calls IMPLEMENTATION.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD responses_two_calls_brace_in_src.\\\\n    DATA lv_body TYPE string.\\\\n    lv_body =\\\\n      '{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"resp_1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"output\\\\\\\":[' \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      '{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"function_call\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"fc_1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"call_id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"c1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"write_source\\\\\\\",' \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      '\\\\\\\"arguments\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ZCL_PIA_DEMO\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"source\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"CLASS z. METHOD m. DATA lv_open TYPE string. lv_open = ''{''. ENDMETHOD.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\",' \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      '\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"},' \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      '{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"function_call\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"fc_2\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"call_id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"c2\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"read_object\\\\\\\",' \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      '\\\\\\\"arguments\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ZCL_PIA_JSON_UTIL\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}' \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      ']}'.\\\\n\\\\n    DATA(lt_calls) = zcl_pia_00_llm_http=\\u003eparse_calls_responses( lv_body ).\\\\n\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = 2 act = lines( lt_calls )\\\\n      msg = 'both function_call items must be parsed' ).\\\\n\\\\n    READ TABLE lt_calls INDEX 1 INTO DATA(ls_first).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals( exp = 'c1'           act = ls_first-id ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals( exp = 'write_source' act = ls_first-name ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = '{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ZCL_PIA_DEMO\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"source\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"CLASS z. METHOD m. DATA lv_open TYPE string. lv_open = ''{''. ENDMETHOD.\\\\\\\"}'\\\\n      act = ls_first-arguments\\\\n      msg = 'arguments must end at the JSON end: no trailing call_id/status text' ).\\\\n\\\\n    READ TABLE lt_calls INDEX 2 INTO DATA(ls_second).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals( exp = 'c2'          act = ls_second-id ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals( exp = 'read_object' act = ls_second-name ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = '{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ZCL_PIA_JSON_UTIL\\\\\\\"}' act = ls_second-arguments ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD chat_two_calls_brace_in_src.\\\\n    DATA lv_body TYPE string.\\\\n    lv_body =\\\\n      '{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"chat_1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"choices\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"index\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"message\\\\\\\":{' \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      '\\\\\\\"role\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"assistant\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"content\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"tool_calls\\\\\\\":[' \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      '{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"c1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"function\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"function\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"write_source\\\\\\\",' \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      '\\\\\\\"arguments\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ZCL_X\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"source\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"m1. lv_open = ''{''.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\"}},' \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      '{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"c2\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"function\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"function\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"read_object\\\\\\\",' \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      '\\\\\\\"arguments\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ZCL_Y\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\"}}' \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      ']}}]}'.\\\\n\\\\n    DATA(lt_calls) = zcl_pia_00_llm_http=\\u003eparse_calls_chat( lv_body ).\\\\n\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = 2 act = lines( lt_calls )\\\\n      msg = 'both tool_calls entries must be parsed' ).\\\\n\\\\n    READ TABLE lt_calls INDEX 1 INTO DATA(ls_first).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals( exp = 'write_source' act = ls_first-name ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = '{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ZCL_X\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"source\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"m1. lv_open = ''{''.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'.act = ls_first-arguments ) ##NO_TEXT.\\\\n\\\\n    READ TABLE lt_calls INDEX 2 INTO DATA(ls_second).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals( exp = 'read_object' act = ls_second-name ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals( exp = '{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ZCL_Y\\\\\\\"}' act = ls_second-arguments ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD split_entries_skips_strings.\\\\n    \\\\\\\" braces inside string values must not open/close an entry\\\\n    DATA(lt_) = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003esplit_entries(\\\\n      '[{\\\\\\\"a\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"x{y\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"b\\\\\\\":1},{\\\\\\\"c\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"d\\\\\\\":2}]' ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = 2 act = lines( lt_ ) msg = 'two entries expected' ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals( exp = '{\\\\\\\"a\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"x{y\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"b\\\\\\\":1}' act = lt_[ 1 ] ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals( exp = '{\\\\\\\"c\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"d\\\\\\\":2}'   act = lt_[ 2 ] ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD balanced_skips_strings.\\\\n    \\\\\\\" brackets/braces inside string values must not count towards the depth\\\\n    DATA(lv_arr) = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eextract_balanced(\\\\n      iv_json = '{\\\\\\\"items\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"a[b\\\\\\\"]}' iv_key = 'items' iv_open = '[' iv_close = ']' ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals( exp = '[\\\\\\\"a[b\\\\\\\"]' act = lv_arr ).\\\\n\\\\n    DATA(lv_obj) = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eextract_balanced(\\\\n      iv_json = '{\\\\\\\"obj\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"s\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"a{b\\\\\\\"}}' iv_key = 'obj' iv_open = '{' iv_close = '}' ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals( exp = '{\\\\\\\"s\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"a{b\\\\\\\"}' act = lv_obj ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\nENDCLASS.\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_-7228016130479092023\",\"id\":\"fc_call_-7228016130479092023\",\"name\":\"write_source\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"}],\"parallel_tool_calls\":true,\"previous_response_id\":\"\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":20934,\"input_tokens_details\":{\"cached_tokens\":18688},\"output_tokens\":11922,\"output_tokens_details\":{\"reasoning_tokens\":10424},\"total_tokens\":32856}}
{\"conversation_id\":\"\",\"created_at\":1791373953,\"error\":null,\"id\":\"resp_2026100719512851bf29ccb9c844c5\",\"incomplete_details\":null,\"instructions\":\"You are PIA (Pi-ABAP Agent), written in ABAP, running on the model glm-5.3 (z.ai) through backend OSG-STORE. If asked which model you are, say exactly that; never claim another model or vendor. Tools: read_object(name), write_source(name, source - FULL source, include main|testclasses), activate(name), run_tests(name). Rules: read before write; write full source; always activate after write; if activation says publish pending, finish the turn and run_tests in the next turn. Answer briefly in the user language. Your own code: ZCL_PIA_00_EXECUTOR (agent loop), ZCL_PIA_00_LLM_HTTP (LLM client: builds requests, parses responses and tool calls), ZCL_PIA_00_JSON_UTIL (JSON helpers), ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION and ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION_STORE (conversation), ZCL_PIA_00_REGISTRY (tools), ZCL_PIA_15_T_* (the tools), ZCL_PIA_20_B_* (backends), ZCL_PIA_30_* (terminal, turns). Unit tests live in the testclasses include of a class.\",\"metadata\":null,\"model\":\"glm-5.3\",\"object\":\"response\",\"output\":[{\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Hmm, it seems the write_source call went out without parameters content \u2014 that's odd. Possibly the parameters were stripped. The result says \\\"written ZCL_PIA_00_LLM_HTTP testclasses (4579 chars)\\\". But I didn't provide source... The environment may have filled it? That's concerning \u2014 I must not rely on that. Let me now explicitly write the test source I intend.\\n\\nI need to compose the test include for ZCL_PIA_00_LLM_HTTP:\\n\\n```abap\\nCLASS ltcl_parse_calls DEFINITION FINAL FOR TESTING\\n  DURATION SHORT\\n  RISK LEVEL HARMLESS.\\n\\n  PRIVATE SECTION.\\n    METHODS responses_two_calls_brace_in_string FOR TESTING\\n      RAISING cx_static_check.\\n    METHODS chat_two_calls_brace_in_string FOR TESTING\\n      RAISING cx_static_check.\\nENDCLASS.\\n\\nCLASS ltcl_parse_calls IMPLEMENTATION.\\n\\n  METHOD responses_two_calls_brace_in_string.\\n    \\\" regression: a '{' inside a string literal of the first call's source made\\n    \\\" split_entries swallow the second entry and let extract_balanced run past\\n    \\\" the arguments value (\\\",\\\"call_id\\\":\\\"c1\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"})\\n    DATA lv_body TYPE string.\\n    DATA lv_src TYPE string.\\n    lv_src = 'CLASS zcl_x DEFINITION.' \\u0026\\u0026 |\\\\n| \\u0026\\u0026\\n             '  METHODS m.' \\u0026\\u0026 |\\\\n| \\u0026\\u0026\\n             '  DATA lv_open TYPE string.' \\u0026\\u0026 |\\\\n| \\u0026\\u0026\\n             '  METHOD m. lv_open = ''{''. ENDMETHOD.' \\u0026\\u0026 |\\\\n| \\u0026\\u0026\\n             'ENDCLASS.'.\\n    DATA lv_args TYPE string.\\n    lv_args = '{\\\"name\\\":\\\"ZCL_X\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"' \\u0026\\u0026 lv_src \\u0026\\u0026 '\\\"}'.\\n\\n    lv_body = '{\\\"id\\\":\\\"resp_1\\\",\\\"output\\\":[' \\u0026\\u0026\\n              '{\\\"type\\\":\\\"function_call\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"fc_1\\\",\\\"call_id\\\":\\\"c1\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"write_source\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":' \\u0026\\u0026\\n              '\\\"' \\u0026\\u0026 escape( lv_args ) \\u0026\\u0026 '\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"},' \\u0026\\u0026\\n              '{\\\"type\\\":\\\"function_call\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"fc_2\\\",\\\"call_id\\\":\\\"c2\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"read_object\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":' \\u0026\\u0026\\n              '\\\"' \\u0026\\u0026 escape( '{\\\"name\\\":\\\"ZCL_Y\\\"}' ) \\u0026\\u0026 '\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}' \\u0026\\u0026\\n              ']}'.\\n\\n    DATA(lt_calls) = zcl_pia_00_llm_http=\\u003eparse_calls_responses( lv_body ).\\n\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals( exp = 2 act = lines( lt_calls ) msg = 'both calls must be parsed' ).\\n    ...\\n```\\n\\nHmm wait: escape() escapes newline as \\\\n and `\\\"` as `\\\\\\\"` \u2014 that mimics the model's JSON encoding of arguments. Note: escape does NOT escape `'` (no need). And `{` stays raw. Good \u2014 this reproduces the bug: the `'{''` produces a raw `{` inside the arguments JSON string.\\n\\nBut hold on \u2014 I should double-check what escape does to `\\\\n`: yes `\\\\n`. And the PCRE extract_str handles `\\\\\\\\.` escapes. Good.\\n\\nAssertions:\\n- lines = 2\\n- call 1: id = c1, name = write_source, arguments = lv_args (the inner JSON with `'{''` intact, unescaped).\\n- call 2: id = c2, name = read_object, arguments = `{\\\"name\\\":\\\"ZCL_Y\\\"}`.\\n\\nFor chat format body:\\n\\n```json\\n{\\\"id\\\":\\\"chatcmpl-1\\\",\\\"choices\\\":[{\\\"index\\\":0,\\\"message\\\":{\\\"role\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"content\\\":null,\\\"tool_calls\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"c1\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"function\\\",\\\"function\\\":{\\\"name\\\":\\\"write_source\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":\\\"{...with '{' ...}\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"c2\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"function\\\",\\\"function\\\":{\\\"name\\\":\\\"read_object\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":\\\"{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ZCL_Y\\\\\\\"}\\\"}}]},\\\"finish_reason\\\":\\\"tool_calls\\\"}]}\\n```\\n\\nparse_calls_chat extracts `tool_calls` array then per entry extract_str id/name + balanced arguments. Same bug.\\n\\nAlso maybe a direct split_entries test would be in JSON_UTIL, but I can't safely write there (can't read existing testclasses; overwriting would destroy ESCAPE_EMOJI_PAIR). The LLM_HTTP-level tests cover both split_entries and the arguments extraction. Good \u2014 and note run_tests on JSON_UTIL will still be runnable read-only to verify no regression (it runs on active code; my JSON_UTIL main-include change will be activated too).\\n\\nWait \u2014 but if I change ZCL_PIA_00_JSON_UTIL main include, activation of JSON_UTIL doesn't touch its testclasses include. Good, ESCAPE_EMOJI_PAIR preserved.\\n\\nAlso should I verify red BEFORE the fix: write test, activate LLM_HTTP, run tests \u2192 new tests red (2 fails), ESCAPE_EMOJI_PAIR untouched. Then fix JSON_UTIL + LLM_HTTP main, activate both, run tests \u2192 green (except emoji in JSON_UTIL which stays red).\\n\\nImportant: the tests must fail for the right reason (argument overrun + lost second call). Let me double check the current buggy behavior produces lines=1: as analyzed, split_entries merges both entries into one \u2192 1 call. assert lines=2 fails \u2192 RED. \\n\\nNow, about the mysterious parameterless write_source that \\\"succeeded\\\" with 4579 chars \u2014 unknown content. I must rewrite with explicit source now. Then activate.\\n\\nLet me write the full testclasses source carefully.\\n\\n```abap\\nCLASS ltcl_parse_calls DEFINITION FINAL FOR TESTING\\n  DURATION SHORT\\n  RISK LEVEL HARMLESS.\\n\\n  PRIVATE SECTION.\\n    METHODS brace_in_string_two_calls_responses FOR TESTING\\n      RAISING cx_static_check.\\n    METHODS brace_in_string_two_calls_chat FOR TESTING\\n      RAISING cx_static_check.\\nENDCLASS.\\n\\nCLASS ltcl_parse_calls IMPLEMENTATION.\\n\\n  METHOD brace_in_string_two_calls_responses.\\n    DATA:\\n      lv_src    TYPE string,\\n      lv_args1  TYPE string,\\n      lv_body   TYPE string.\\n\\n    lv_src =\\n      `CLASS zcl_x DEFINITION.` \\u0026\\u0026 |\\\\n| \\u0026\\u0026\\n      `  METHOD m.` \\u0026\\u0026 |\\\\n| \\u0026\\u0026\\n      `    lv_open = '{'.` \\u0026\\u0026 |\\\\n| \\u0026\\u0026\\n      `  ENDMETHOD.` \\u0026\\u0026 |\\\\n| \\u0026\\u0026\\n      `ENDCLASS.`.\\n\\n    lv_args1 = `{\\\"name\\\":\\\"ZCL_X\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"` \\u0026\\u0026 lv_src \\u0026\\u0026 `\\\"}`.\\n\\n    lv_body =\\n      `{\\\"id\\\":\\\"resp_1\\\",\\\"object\\\":\\\"response\\\",\\\"output\\\":[` \\u0026\\u0026\\n      `{\\\"type\\\":\\\"function_call\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"fc_1\\\",\\\"call_id\\\":\\\"c1\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"write_source\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":\\\"` \\u0026\\u0026\\n      zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eescape( lv_args1 ) \\u0026\\u0026 `\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"},` \\u0026\\u0026\\n      `{\\\"type\\\":\\\"function_call\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"fc_2\\\",\\\"call_id\\\":\\\"c2\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"read_object\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":\\\"` \\u0026\\u0026\\n      zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eescape( `{\\\"name\\\":\\\"ZCL_Y\\\"}` ) \\u0026\\u0026 `\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}` \\u0026\\u0026\\n      `]}`.\\n\\n    DATA(lt_calls) = zcl_pia_00_llm_http=\\u003eparse_calls_responses( lv_body ).\\n\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\n        exp  = 2\\n        act  = lines( lt_calls )\\n        msg  = 'a brace inside a string literal must not swallow the second call' ).\\n\\n    READ TABLE lt_calls INDEX 1 INTO DATA(ls_first).\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\n        exp = 'c1'  act = ls_first-id ).\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\n        exp = 'write_source' act = ls_first-name ).\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\n        exp  = lv_args1\\n        act  = ls_first-arguments\\n        msg  = 'arguments must end at the JSON value, no trailing fields' ).\\n\\n    READ TABLE lt_calls INDEX 2 INTO DATA(ls_second).\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals( exp = 'c2' act = ls_second-id ).\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals( exp = 'read_object' act = ls_second-name ).\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals( exp = `{\\\"name\\\":\\\"ZCL_Y\\\"}` act = ls_second-arguments ).\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\n```\\n\\nCareful with READ TABLE ... INTO DATA(...) \u2014 inline DATA in READ TABLE is allowed in newer ABAP (7.40+): `READ TABLE lt_calls INDEX 1 INTO DATA(ls_first).` Yes, allowed.\\n\\nFor chat:\\n\\n```abap\\n  METHOD brace_in_string_two_calls_chat.\\n    ... lv_body =\\n      `{\\\"id\\\":\\\"chatcmpl-1\\\",\\\"object\\\":\\\"chat.completion\\\",\\\"choices\\\":[{\\\"index\\\":0,` \\u0026\\u0026\\n      `\\\"message\\\":{\\\"role\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"content\\\":null,\\\"tool_calls\\\":[` \\u0026\\u0026\\n      `{\\\"id\\\":\\\"c1\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"function\\\",\\\"function\\\":{\\\"name\\\":\\\"write_source\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":\\\"` \\u0026\\u0026\\n      escape( lv_args1 ) \\u0026\\u0026 `\\\"}},` \\u0026\\u0026\\n      `{\\\"id\\\":\\\"c2\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"function\\\",\\\"function\\\":{\\\"name\\\":\\\"read_object\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":\\\"` \\u0026\\u0026\\n      escape( `{\\\"name\\\":\\\"ZCL_Y\\\"}` ) \\u0026\\u0026 `\\\"}}` \\u0026\\u0026\\n      `]},\\\"finish_reason\\\":\\\"tool_calls\\\"}]}`.\\n```\\n\\nparse_calls_chat: extract_balanced body key 'tool_calls' open '[' \u2014 note the body contains `[` ... fine; then `]` of tool_calls array... wait, careful: the outer body also has `]}` at end (choices array). extract_balanced finds first `\\\"`tool_calls\\\"` \u2014 hmm, `FIND lv_pat IN iv_json` \u2014 the pattern `\\\"tool_calls\\\"` \u2014 first occurrence in body. The string `\\\"tool_calls\\\"` appears in \\\"finish_reason\\\":\\\"tool_calls\\\" too, but the first occurrence is the key. OK. Then finds first `[` after \u2014 the tool_calls array. Depth counting on `[`/`]`: inside, there are no other brackets... the arguments contain none. Ends at the `]` before `}`. But there's `\\\"finish_reason\\\":\\\"tool_calls\\\"` AFTER \u2014 not bracket chars. OK.\\n\\nThen split_entries on the array content: entries merged due to bug \u2192 1 entry. RED as expected.\\n\\nAssertions same as responses.\\n\\nBoth tests RAISING cx_static_check \u2014 none needed really, but assert doesn't raise... cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals doesn't raise cx_static_check (it fails the test). Actually in newer versions assert methods have no RAISING. Keep RAISING cx_static_check anyway \u2014 harmless? If a method doesn't raise, declaring RAISING cx_static_check is fine.\\n\\nHmm, one concern: `zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eescape( lv_args1 )` inside string concatenation with \\u0026\\u0026 \u2014 method call in expression: allowed (functional method call in string template expression with \\u0026\\u0026). Yes.\\n\\nBut wait \u2014 the previous mystery write already wrote 4579 chars to the testclasses include of LLM_HTTP and it's not activated yet. I'll overwrite with my explicit source and then activate.\\n\\nOne more check on the fix design for extract_balanced case B via extract_str: in parse_calls_chat, arguments extraction becomes:\\n\\n```abap\\nls-arguments = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eunescape(\\n    zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eextract_str( iv_json = lv_e iv_name = 'arguments' ) ).\\nIF ls-arguments IS INITIAL.\\n  ls-arguments = zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eunescape( zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eextract_balanced(\\n                   iv_json = lv_e iv_key = 'arguments' iv_open = '{' iv_close = '}' ) ).\\nENDIF.\\n```\\n\\nHmm \u2014 is fallback needed? If some producer sends arguments as a real object `{\\\"name\\\":...}` (not a string), extract_str fails (no `\\\"arguments\\\"` followed by `\\\"`... actually the PCRE requires `:\\\"` \u2014 an object value would not match \u2192 empty). Fallback to balanced extraction keeps compatibility. I'll include the fallback in both parse methods. Reasonable.\\n\\nBut careful: extract_str PCRE `\\\"arguments\\\"\\\\s*:\\\\s*\\\"...\\\"` \u2014 for the entry text of the SECOND call it extracts its own arguments \u2014 since we now split entries correctly, each lv_e is one call's object. Good.\\n\\nAlso there's `build_input_items` \u2014 already uses extract_str. Good.\\n\\nNow split_entries fix (string-aware):\\n\\n```abap\\n  METHOD split_entries.\\n    DATA lv_len_arr TYPE i.\\n    lv_len_arr = strlen( iv_arr ).\\n    DATA lv_pos TYPE i VALUE 0.\\n    WHILE lv_pos \\u003c lv_len_arr.\\n      FIND FIRST OCCURRENCE OF '{' IN iv_arr+lv_pos MATCH OFFSET DATA(lv_off).\\n      IF sy-subrc \\u003c\\u003e 0. EXIT. ENDIF.\\n      DATA lv_start TYPE i.\\n      lv_start = lv_pos + lv_off.\\n      IF lv_start \\u003e= lv_len_arr. EXIT. ENDIF.\\n      DATA lv_depth TYPE i.\\n      lv_depth = 1.\\n      DATA lv_end TYPE i.\\n      lv_end = lv_start.\\n      DATA lv_str TYPE abap_bool.\\n      lv_str = abap_false.\\n      WHILE lv_end \\u003c lv_len_arr - 1 AND lv_depth \\u003e 0.\\n        lv_end = lv_end + 1.\\n        DATA lv_ch TYPE string.\\n        lv_ch = iv_arr+lv_end(1).\\n        IF lv_str = abap_true.\\n          IF lv_ch = `\\\\`.\\n            lv_end = lv_end + 1. \\\" skip escaped char\\n          ELSEIF lv_ch = `\\\"`.\\n            lv_str = abap_false.\\n          ENDIF.\\n        ELSEIF lv_ch = `\\\"`.\\n          lv_str = abap_true.\\n        ELSEIF lv_ch = '{'.\\n          lv_depth = lv_depth + 1.\\n        ELSEIF lv_ch = '}'.\\n          lv_depth = lv_depth - 1.\\n        ENDIF.\\n      ENDWHILE.\\n      ...\\n```\\n\\nWait \u2014 existing test BALANCED_UNCLOSED expects something for unclosed input; with depth\\u003e0 \u2192 lv_end = len-1 \u2192 entry = rest. Preserved.\\n\\nNote existing behavior details I must preserve:\\n- BALANCED_NESTED_AND_ARRAY passes currently; my change keeps correctness.\\n- Escaped char at last position: `iv_arr+lv_end(1)` access when lv_end = lv_len_arr after skip? If `\\\\` is the last char, lv_end+1 = lv_len_arr \u2192 next WHILE check `lv_end \\u003c lv_len_arr - 1` false \u2192 exit loop; then lv_end used for substring: lv_len = lv_end - lv_start + 1 could exceed bounds \u2192 existing clamp `IF lv_start + lv_len \\u003e lv_len_arr. lv_len = lv_len_arr - lv_start.` handles. OK. But if lv_end = lv_len_arr (beyond last index)... the clamp uses lv_len_arr - lv_start, fine.\\n\\nAlso `DATA lv_ch` inside loop \u2014 DATA declarations in loops are fine (declared once).\\n\\nextract_balanced fix similarly:\\n\\n```abap\\n  METHOD extract_balanced.\\n    DATA lv_off TYPE i.\\n    DATA(lv_pat) = '\\\"' \\u0026\\u0026 iv_key \\u0026\\u0026 '\\\"'.\\n    FIND lv_pat IN iv_json MATCH OFFSET lv_off.\\n    IF sy-subrc \\u003c\\u003e 0. RETURN. ENDIF.\\n    DATA lv_rest TYPE string.\\n    lv_rest = iv_json+lv_off.\\n    DATA lv_start TYPE i.\\n    FIND FIRST OCCURRENCE OF iv_open IN lv_rest MATCH OFFSET lv_start.\\n    IF sy-subrc \\u003c\\u003e 0. RETURN. ENDIF.\\n    \\\" skip to first opening char that is not inside a string? \\n```\\n\\nHmm \u2014 subtle: FIND FIRST `{` after the key could land inside a string value. For key='arguments' with string value: the first `{` is the content brace \u2014 desired start. For robustness generally it's what current code does. Keep.\\n\\nThen depth scan with string-awareness (case A: quotes not escaped toggle):\\n\\n```abap\\n    DATA lv_depth TYPE i VALUE 1.\\n    DATA lv_pos TYPE i.\\n    lv_pos = lv_start.\\n    DATA lv_len TYPE i.\\n    lv_len = strlen( lv_rest ).\\n    DATA lv_str TYPE abap_bool VALUE abap_false.\\n    WHILE lv_pos \\u003c lv_len - 1 AND lv_depth \\u003e 0.\\n      lv_pos = lv_pos + 1.\\n      DATA lv_ch TYPE string.\\n      lv_ch = lv_rest+lv_pos(1).\\n      IF lv_str = abap_true.\\n        IF lv_ch = `\\\\`.\\n          lv_pos = lv_pos + 1.\\n        ELSEIF lv_ch = `\\\"`.\\n          lv_str = abap_false.\\n        ENDIF.\\n      ELSEIF lv_ch = `\\\"`.\\n        lv_str = abap_true.\\n      ELSEIF lv_ch = iv_open.\\n        lv_depth = lv_depth + 1.\\n      ELSEIF lv_ch = iv_close.\\n        lv_depth = lv_depth - 1.\\n      ENDIF.\\n    ENDWHILE.\\n    DATA(lv_l) = lv_pos - lv_start + 1.\\n    rv_ = lv_rest+lv_start(lv_l).\\n```\\n\\nCareful: `WHILE lv_pos \\u003c lv_len - 1` with lv_len possibly 0 \u2192 negative, loop won't run; then lv_l = lv_pos - lv_start + 1 \u2014 original code had same structure with strlen(lv_rest). Original: `WHILE lv_pos \\u003c strlen( lv_rest ) - 1 AND lv_depth \\u003e 0.` and at end `DATA(lv_len) = lv_pos - lv_start + 1. rv_ = lv_rest+lv_start(lv_len).` \u2014 hmm if lv_pos overruns (lv_pos+1 beyond last index after escape skip at end) \u2192 substring could exceed bounds. Original had no clamp! If lv_pos = lv_len (one past last index possible after skip), lv_l = lv_len - lv_start + 1 \u2192 substring beyond end \u2192 dump. Edge case; add clamp like split_entries: if lv_start + lv_l \\u003e lv_len, lv_l = lv_len - lv_start. Safe. But must preserve BALANCED_UNCLOSED semantics: unclosed \u2192 returns rest of string. With clamp: lv_pos ends at lv_len-1 \u2192 lv_l = lv_len-1 - lv_start + 1 = lv_len - lv_start \u2192 whole rest. Same as before. Good.\\n\\nOne more consideration: escape-skip when lv_ch = `\\\\` and next char exists; simply lv_pos = lv_pos + 1; loop then increments again at top. If that puts lv_pos \\u003e= lv_len-1, loop exits \u2014 fine.\\n\\nNow \u2014 does making extract_balanced string-aware break existing passing tests? BALANCED_OBJECT, BALANCED_NESTED_AND_ARRAY, BALANCED_MISSING_KEY, BALANCED_NO_OPEN_BRACKET, BALANCED_UNCLOSED \u2014 presumably simple cases without quotes; string-awareness only changes behavior when `\\\"` present. Likely still green. Will verify by running JSON_UTIL tests after fix (expect only ESCAPE_EMOJI_PAIR red).\\n\\nAnd parse_calls_chat/responses: arguments via extract_str. For the responses test entry: `\\\"arguments\\\":\\\"{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\"...}\\\"` \u2192 extract_str PCRE matches the escaped string \u2192 unescape \u2192 lv_args1. \\n\\nBut WAIT \u2014 one important check in parse_calls_chat: entry `{\\\"id\\\":\\\"c1\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"function\\\",\\\"function\\\":{\\\"name\\\":\\\"write_source\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":\\\"...\\\"}}`. extract_str(iv_json=lv_e, iv_name='arguments') \u2192 PCRE `\\\"arguments\\\"\\\\s*:\\\\s*\\\"((?:[^\\\"\\\\\\\\]|\\\\\\\\.)*)\\\"` \u2192 matches. Good. ls-name from extract_str 'name' \u2014 first occurrence of `\\\"name\\\"` in entry \u2014 inside function object. fine.\\n\\nFor responses entry: `{\\\"type\\\":\\\"function_call\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"fc_1\\\",\\\"call_id\\\":\\\"c1\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"write_source\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":\\\"...\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}` \u2014 extract_str 'name' \u2192 \\\"write_source\\\" (first `\\\"name\\\"` is the key... wait `\\\"name\\\"` \u2014 hmm, the PCRE `\\\"name\\\"\\\\s*:\\\\s*\\\"...\\\"` \u2014 could it match `\\\"call_id\\\":\\\"c1\\\",\\\"name\\\"...`? It finds `\\\"name\\\":\\\"write_source\\\"` \u2014 but also earlier: is there any `\\\"name\\\"` substring before? `\\\"function_call\\\"` contains... no. OK.\\n\\nHmm, one gotcha: in the responses entry, key `\\\"name\\\"` appears also INSIDE arguments (`{\\\"name\\\":\\\"ZCL_X\\\"...}`) \u2014 but first match is the outer one at earlier offset. extract_str uses FIND FIRST OCCURRENCE \u2014 outer comes first. Good.\\n\\nNow also double check: the executor pushes assistant raw etc. \u2014 unchanged.\\n\\nAlright. Also the mystery write: I'll just overwrite with explicit source. Then activate LLM_HTTP, run tests \u2192 expect 2 red (new tests) \u2014 wait, activation makes new code live NEXT step; run_tests runs on published active code. So after activate, if it says publish pending, finish turn; next turn run tests. Let me do: write testclasses (explicit), activate. Then next turn run_tests LLM_HTTP \u2192 expect RED (2 fails). Then write fixes (JSON_UTIL main + LLM_HTTP main), activate both, then run tests \u2192 green + emoji red in JSON_UTIL.\\n\\nActually, to show red cleanly, order matters: tests must run against ACTIVE code that still has the bug. Since run_tests uses published code, and my testclasses write needs activation+publish first. So: turn A: write testclasses, activate. Turn B: run_tests \u2192 red. Turn C: write fixed mains, activate both. Turn D: run tests both \u2192 green/expected.\\n\\nLet me now write the explicit testclasses source.\",\"type\":\"reasoning_text\"}],\"encrypted_content\":null,\"id\":\"rs_2026100719512851bf29ccb9c844c5\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":[],\"type\":\"reasoning\"},{\"content\":[{\"annotations\":[],\"text\":\"The blank write went through with unknown content \u2013 I must overwrite it explicitly with my intended test source before activating anything.\",\"type\":\"output_text\"}],\"id\":\"msg_2026100719512851bf29ccb9c844c5\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"message\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"include\\\":\\\"testclasses\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"ZCL_PIA_00_LLM_HTTP\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"\\\\\\\"* Regression tests for tool-call parsing (see parse_calls_chat / parse_calls_responses)\\\\n\\\\\\\"* Bug: a '{' inside a string literal of the first call's arguments (e.g. lv_open = '{'.)\\\\n\\\\\\\"* made the brace-counting scan overrun the arguments value (extra text\\\\n\\\\\\\"* '\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"call_id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"c1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}') and swallow the second call.\\\\nCLASS ltcl_parse_calls DEFINITION FINAL FOR TESTING\\\\n  DURATION SHORT\\\\n  RISK LEVEL HARMLESS.\\\\n\\\\n  PRIVATE SECTION.\\\\n    METHODS responses_two_calls_brace_in_string FOR TESTING\\\\n      RAISING cx_static_check.\\\\n    METHODS chat_two_calls_brace_in_string FOR TESTING\\\\n      RAISING cx_static_check.\\\\nENDCLASS.\\\\n\\\\nCLASS ltcl_parse_calls IMPLEMENTATION.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD responses_two_calls_brace_in_string.\\\\n    DATA lv_src TYPE string.\\\\n    DATA lv_args1 TYPE string.\\\\n    DATA lv_body TYPE string.\\\\n\\\\n    lv_src = `CLASS zcl_x DEFINITION.` \\u0026\\u0026 |\\\\\\\\n| \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n             `  METHOD m.` \\u0026\\u0026 |\\\\\\\\n| \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n             `    lv_open = '{'.` \\u0026\\u0026 |\\\\\\\\n| \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n             `  ENDMETHOD.` \\u0026\\u0026 |\\\\\\\\n| \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n             `ENDCLASS.`.\\\\n\\\\n    lv_args1 = `{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ZCL_X\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"source\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"` \\u0026\\u0026 lv_src \\u0026\\u0026 `\\\\\\\"}`.\\\\n\\\\n    lv_body = `{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"resp_1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"object\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"response\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"output\\\\\\\":[` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n              `{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"function_call\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"fc_1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"call_id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"c1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"write_source\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"arguments\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n              zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eescape( lv_args1 ) \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n              `\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"},` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n              `{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"function_call\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"fc_2\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"call_id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"c2\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"read_object\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"arguments\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n              zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eescape( `{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ZCL_Y\\\\\\\"}` ) \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n              `\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n              `]}`.\\\\n\\\\n    DATA(lt_calls) = zcl_pia_00_llm_http=\\u003eparse_calls_responses( lv_body ).\\\\n\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n        exp = 2\\\\n        act = lines( lt_calls )\\\\n        msg = 'a brace inside a string literal must not swallow the second call' ).\\\\n\\\\n    READ TABLE lt_calls INDEX 1 INTO DATA(ls_first).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals( exp = 'c1' act = ls_first-id ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals( exp = 'write_source' act = ls_first-name ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n        exp = lv_args1\\\\n        act = ls_first-arguments\\\\n        msg = 'arguments must end with the JSON value, no trailing fields' ).\\\\n\\\\n    READ TABLE lt_calls INDEX 2 INTO DATA(ls_second).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals( exp = 'c2' act = ls_second-id ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals( exp = 'read_object' act = ls_second-name ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals( exp = `{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ZCL_Y\\\\\\\"}` act = ls_second-arguments ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD chat_two_calls_brace_in_string.\\\\n    DATA lv_src TYPE string.\\\\n    DATA lv_args1 TYPE string.\\\\n    DATA lv_body TYPE string.\\\\n\\\\n    lv_src = `CLASS zcl_x DEFINITION.` \\u0026\\u0026 |\\\\\\\\n| \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n             `  METHOD m.` \\u0026\\u0026 |\\\\\\\\n| \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n             `    lv_open = '{'.` \\u0026\\u0026 |\\\\\\\\n| \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n             `  ENDMETHOD.` \\u0026\\u0026 |\\\\\\\\n| \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n             `ENDCLASS.`.\\\\n\\\\n    lv_args1 = `{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ZCL_X\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"source\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"` \\u0026\\u0026 lv_src \\u0026\\u0026 `\\\\\\\"}`.\\\\n\\\\n    lv_body = `{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"chatcmpl-1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"object\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"chat.completion\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"choices\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"index\\\\\\\":0,` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n              `\\\\\\\"message\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"role\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"assistant\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"content\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"tool_calls\\\\\\\":[` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n              `{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"c1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"function\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"function\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"write_source\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"arguments\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n              zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eescape( lv_args1 ) \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n              `\\\\\\\"}},` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n              `{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"c2\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"function\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"function\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"read_object\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"arguments\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n              zcl_pia_00_json_util=\\u003eescape( `{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ZCL_Y\\\\\\\"}` ) \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n              `\\\\\\\"}}` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n              `]},\\\\\\\"finish_reason\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"tool_calls\\\\\\\"}]}`.\\\\n\\\\n    DATA(lt_calls) = zcl_pia_00_llm_http=\\u003eparse_calls_chat( lv_body ).\\\\n\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n        exp = 2\\\\n        act = lines( lt_calls )\\\\n        msg = 'a brace inside a string literal must not swallow the second call' ).\\\\n\\\\n    READ TABLE lt_calls INDEX 1 INTO DATA(ls_first).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals( exp = 'c1' act = ls_first-id ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals( exp = 'write_source' act = ls_first-name ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n        exp = lv_args1\\\\n        act = ls_first-arguments\\\\n        msg = 'arguments must end with the JSON value, no trailing fields' ).\\\\n\\\\n    READ TABLE lt_calls INDEX 2 INTO DATA(ls_second).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals( exp = 'c2' act = ls_second-id ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals( exp = 'read_object' act = ls_second-name ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals( exp = `{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ZCL_Y\\\\\\\"}` act = ls_second-arguments ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\nENDCLASS.\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_-7228011663713105296\",\"id\":\"fc_call_-7228011663713105296\",\"name\":\"write_source\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"}],\"parallel_tool_calls\":true,\"previous_response_id\":\"\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":20973,\"input_tokens_details\":{\"cached_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":5757,\"output_tokens_details\":{\"reasoning_tokens\":4512},\"total_tokens\":26730}}
