{\"conversation_id\":\"\",\"created_at\":1791374023,\"error\":null,\"id\":\"resp_2026100719531311973454f24b45cf\",\"incomplete_details\":null,\"instructions\":\"You are PIA (Pi-ABAP Agent), written in ABAP, running on the model glm-5.3 (z.ai) through backend OSG-STORE. If asked which model you are, say exactly that; never claim another model or vendor. Tools: read_object(name), write_source(name, source - FULL source, include main|testclasses), activate(name), run_tests(name). Rules: read before write; write full source; always activate after write; if activation says publish pending, finish the turn and run_tests in the next turn. Answer briefly in the user language. Your own code: ZCL_PIA_00_EXECUTOR (agent loop), ZCL_PIA_00_LLM_HTTP (LLM client: builds requests, parses responses and tool calls), ZCL_PIA_00_JSON_UTIL (JSON helpers), ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION and ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION_STORE (conversation), ZCL_PIA_00_REGISTRY (tools), ZCL_PIA_15_T_* (the tools), ZCL_PIA_20_B_* (backends), ZCL_PIA_30_* (terminal, turns). Unit tests live in the testclasses include of a class.\",\"metadata\":null,\"model\":\"glm-5.3\",\"object\":\"response\",\"output\":[{\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Odd: 0 test classes ran even though I wrote testclasses. Maybe the activation with only a testclasses include didn't take effect, or the write of the testclasses include requires the class to have the \\\"test classes\\\" flag... Or maybe my second write_source (4464 chars) overwrote the first (4579) \u2014 I actually intended only one write; the transcript shows two write_source calls with no parameters displayed. I need to check what's actually in the testclasses include now. I can't read the testclasses include with read_object (it reads main include only, per the description). Let me re-read the class to check... read_object returns definition+implementation (main). Hmm.\\n\\nPerhaps the issue: the local test class must be included properly, e.g. the include needs \\\"CLASS ltc_... DEFINITION ... ENDCLASS.\\\" plus FOR TESTING etc. Maybe the tool didn't attach because the class has no testclass include flag yet, or the write silently produced empty? Or run_tests ran before publish... but it said \\\"GREEN tests ran\\\" now with generation_id dd7eebed \u2014 same generation id as before. Interesting: generation_id \\\"dd7eebed6a18805d\\\" appears in earlier runs too \u2014 that's the currently published generation. The activation said \\\"publish pending \u2014 new code live in next step\\\". Several turns have passed; the run now says GREEN with 0 methods, meaning no test classes found in the published generation... but wait, the same generation id dd7eebed as the pre-activation runs suggests the publish never happened? Or generation ids are per system run.\\n\\nHmm, \\\"expected_generation\\\":null. The activation op_id was returned. Maybe publish takes a turn \u2014 it's been several turns. The run shows 0 classes, so either the testclasses include is empty/not compiled, or the publish didn't include it.\\n\\nLet me try writing the testclasses again (carefully, with parameters this time) and then activate, and also verify by reading... I cannot read testclasses. Alternative: put the test into the testclasses include of ZCL_PIA_00_JSON_UTIL? Same problem.\\n\\nWait \u2014 maybe the issue is different: maybe run_tests only picks up test classes if the main class has the WITH TEST CLASSES property or the include is referenced. Actually in abapGit/ADT, the testclasses include is part of the class object automatically. If I wrote it correctly, activation should compile it. Unless my source had a syntax error and activation... it said \\\"activated\\\" successfully.\\n\\nBut 0 methods ran. Two possibilities: (a) publish didn't happen yet; (b) the test include content got overwritten by my second (shorter, possibly truncated/empty?) write. The second write reported 4464 chars vs 4579 first. I don't know what I actually sent in those calls (parameters not shown in transcript). Dangerous.\\n\\nLet me rewrite the testclasses include now with a known-good source, activate, and run tests next turn. I'll also add a `FOR TESTING` class with proper structure and a `test` method reproducing the bug.\\n\\nPlan for the test (red first):\\n- ltcl_parse DEFINITION FOR TESTING.\\n  METHOD parse_two_calls_brace_in_string.\\n    lv_body = responses-API-like JSON with output array containing two function_call items, first arguments containing source with `'{'` literal.\\n    rt = zcl_pia_00_llm_http=\\u003eparse_calls_responses( lv_body ).\\n    assert lines = 2, second call name present, first arguments contain `'{''` but NOT 'call_id'.\\n\\nExpected red with current code: lines = 1 (merged), arguments contain 'call_id' \u2192 assertion fails.\\n\\nThen fix JSON_UTIL split_entries + extract_balanced (string-aware) and LLM_HTTP arguments extraction via extract_str.\\n\\nLet me write the test now.\",\"type\":\"reasoning_text\"}],\"encrypted_content\":null,\"id\":\"rs_2026100719531311973454f24b45cf\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":[],\"type\":\"reasoning\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"include\\\":\\\"testclasses\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"ZCL_PIA_00_LLM_HTTP\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"*\\\\\\\"--------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\n*\\\\\\\" Bug report: two tool_calls in one assistant message, the source in\\\\n*\\\\\\\" the first arguments contains a single opening brace (lv_open = '{'.)\\\\n*\\\\\\\" -\\u003e only the first call ran, its arguments carried trailing JSON\\\\n*\\\\\\\" (\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"call_id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"c1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}) and the 2nd call was lost.\\\\n*\\\\\\\" Reproduction at parser level (responses + chat wire formats).\\\\n*\\\\\\\"--------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\nCLASS ltcl_parse_calls DEFINITION FINAL\\\\n  FOR TESTING\\\\n  RISK LEVEL HARMLESS\\\\n  DURATION SHORT.\\\\n\\\\n  PRIVATE SECTION.\\\\n    METHODS responses_two_calls_brace_in_string FOR TESTING.\\\\n    METHODS chat_two_calls_brace_in_string FOR TESTING.\\\\n    METHODS responses_plain_two_calls FOR TESTING.\\\\nENDCLASS.\\\\n\\\\nCLASS ltcl_parse_calls IMPLEMENTATION.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD responses_two_calls_brace_in_string.\\\\n    \\\\\\\" wire format: arguments is a JSON string; the source literal '{'\\\\n    \\\\\\\" stays a raw brace inside that string\\\\n    DATA(lv_body) =\\\\n      `{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"resp_1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"output\\\\\\\":[` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      `{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"function_call\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"fc_1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"call_id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"c1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"write_source\\\\\\\",` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      `\\\\\\\"arguments\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ZCL_FOO\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"source\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"CLASS zcl_foo. METHOD run. DATA lv_open TYPE string. lv_open = '{'. ENDMETHOD. ENDCLASS.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\",` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      `\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"},` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      `{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"function_call\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"fc_2\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"call_id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"c2\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"read_object\\\\\\\",` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      `\\\\\\\"arguments\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ZCL_BAR\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}]}`.\\\\n\\\\n    DATA(lt_calls) = zcl_pia_00_llm_http=\\u003eparse_calls_responses( lv_body ).\\\\n\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = 2 act = lines( lt_calls )\\\\n      msg = 'both tool calls must survive the brace inside the string literal' ).\\\\n\\\\n    READ TABLE lt_calls INDEX 1 INTO DATA(ls_first).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_subrc( ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals( exp = 'write_source' act = ls_first-name ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals( exp = 'c1'           act = ls_first-id ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_not_initial( act = ls_first-arguments ).\\\\n    \\\\\\\" the runaway balanced scan swallowed the rest of the item into arguments\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_not_contains(\\\\n      substring = '\\\\\\\"call_id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"c1\\\\\\\"' sub = ls_first-arguments msg = 'arguments must not leak item fields' ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_contains(\\\\n      substring = `lv_open = '{'.` sub = ls_first-arguments msg = 'source literal kept intact' ).\\\\n\\\\n    READ TABLE lt_calls INDEX 2 INTO DATA(ls_second).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_subrc( ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals( exp = 'read_object' act = ls_second-name ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals( exp = 'c2'           act = ls_second-id ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = `{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ZCL_BAR\\\\\\\"}` act = ls_second-arguments ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD chat_two_calls_brace_in_string.\\\\n    DATA(lv_body) =\\\\n      `{\\\\\\\"choices\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"message\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"role\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"assistant\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"tool_calls\\\\\\\":[` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      `{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"c1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"function\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"function\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"write_source\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"arguments\\\\\\\":` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      `\\\\\\\"{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ZCL_FOO\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"source\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"CLASS zcl_foo. METHOD run. DATA lv_open TYPE string. lv_open = '{'. ENDMETHOD. ENDCLASS.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\"}},` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      `{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"c2\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"function\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"function\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"read_object\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"arguments\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ZCL_BAR\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\"}}` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      `]}}]}`.\\\\n\\\\n    DATA(lt_calls) = zcl_pia_00_llm_http=\\u003eparse_calls_chat( lv_body ).\\\\n\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = 2 act = lines( lt_calls )\\\\n      msg = 'both tool calls must survive the brace inside the string literal' ).\\\\n\\\\n    READ TABLE lt_calls INDEX 1 INTO DATA(ls_first).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_subrc( ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals( exp = 'write_source' act = ls_first-name ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_not_contains(\\\\n      substring = '\\\\\\\"function\\\\\\\"' sub = ls_first-arguments msg = 'arguments must not leak item fields' ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_contains(\\\\n      substring = `lv_open = '{'.` sub = ls_first-arguments msg = 'source literal kept intact' ).\\\\n\\\\n    READ TABLE lt_calls INDEX 2 INTO DATA(ls_second).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_subrc( ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals( exp = 'read_object' act = ls_second-name ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = `{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ZCL_BAR\\\\\\\"}` act = ls_second-arguments ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD responses_plain_two_calls.\\\\n    \\\\\\\" regression guard: the ordinary two-call case stays intact\\\\n    DATA(lv_body) =\\\\n      `{\\\\\\\"output\\\\\\\":[` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      `{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"function_call\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"fc_1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"call_id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"c1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"tool_a\\\\\\\",` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      `\\\\\\\"arguments\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"k\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"v\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"},` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      `{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"function_call\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"fc_2\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"call_id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"c2\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"tool_b\\\\\\\",` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      `\\\\\\\"arguments\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"k\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":1}\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}]}`.\\\\n\\\\n    DATA(lt_calls) = zcl_pia_00_llm_http=\\u003eparse_calls_responses( lv_body ).\\\\n\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals( exp = 2 act = lines( lt_calls ) ).\\\\n    READ TABLE lt_calls INDEX 1 INTO DATA(ls_first).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_subrc( ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals( exp = `{\\\\\\\"k\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"v\\\\\\\"}` act = ls_first-arguments ).\\\\n    READ TABLE lt_calls INDEX 2 INTO DATA(ls_second).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_subrc( ).\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals( exp = `{\\\\\\\"k\\\\\\\":1}` act = ls_second-arguments ).\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\nENDCLASS.\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_-7228006578471823097\",\"id\":\"fc_call_-7228006578471823097\",\"name\":\"write_source\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"}],\"parallel_tool_calls\":true,\"previous_response_id\":\"\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":21370,\"input_tokens_details\":{\"cached_tokens\":21248},\"output_tokens\":2191,\"output_tokens_details\":{\"reasoning_tokens\":801},\"total_tokens\":23561}}
{\"conversation_id\":\"\",\"created_at\":1791374028,\"error\":null,\"id\":\"resp_202610071953439470d0c4b91d4189\",\"incomplete_details\":null,\"instructions\":\"You are PIA (Pi-ABAP Agent), written in ABAP, running on the model glm-5.3 (z.ai) through backend OSG-STORE. If asked which model you are, say exactly that; never claim another model or vendor. Tools: read_object(name), write_source(name, source - FULL source, include main|testclasses), activate(name), run_tests(name). Rules: read before write; write full source; always activate after write; if activation says publish pending, finish the turn and run_tests in the next turn. Answer briefly in the user language. Your own code: ZCL_PIA_00_EXECUTOR (agent loop), ZCL_PIA_00_LLM_HTTP (LLM client: builds requests, parses responses and tool calls), ZCL_PIA_00_JSON_UTIL (JSON helpers), ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION and ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION_STORE (conversation), ZCL_PIA_00_REGISTRY (tools), ZCL_PIA_15_T_* (the tools), ZCL_PIA_20_B_* (backends), ZCL_PIA_30_* (terminal, turns). Unit tests live in the testclasses include of a class.\",\"metadata\":null,\"model\":\"glm-5.3\",\"object\":\"response\",\"output\":[{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"name\\\":\\\"ZCL_PIA_00_LLM_HTTP\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_-7228025648126617174\",\"id\":\"fc_call_-7228025648126617174\",\"name\":\"activate\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"}],\"parallel_tool_calls\":true,\"previous_response_id\":\"\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":21409,\"input_tokens_details\":{\"cached_tokens\":21120},\"output_tokens\":19,\"output_tokens_details\":{\"reasoning_tokens\":0},\"total_tokens\":21428}}
{\"conversation_id\":\"\",\"created_at\":1791374063,\"error\":null,\"id\":\"resp_202610071954016836542f490949ed\",\"incomplete_details\":null,\"instructions\":\"You are PIA (Pi-ABAP Agent), written in ABAP, running on the model glm-5.3 (z.ai) through backend OSG-STORE. If asked which model you are, say exactly that; never claim another model or vendor. Tools: read_object(name), write_source(name, source - FULL source, include main|testclasses), activate(name), run_tests(name). Rules: read before write; write full source; always activate after write; if activation says publish pending, finish the turn and run_tests in the next turn. Answer briefly in the user language. Your own code: ZCL_PIA_00_EXECUTOR (agent loop), ZCL_PIA_00_LLM_HTTP (LLM client: builds requests, parses responses and tool calls), ZCL_PIA_00_JSON_UTIL (JSON helpers), ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION and ZCL_PIA_00_SESSION_STORE (conversation), ZCL_PIA_00_REGISTRY (tools), ZCL_PIA_15_T_* (the tools), ZCL_PIA_20_B_* (backends), ZCL_PIA_30_* (terminal, turns). Unit tests live in the testclasses include of a class.\",\"metadata\":null,\"model\":\"glm-5.3\",\"object\":\"response\",\"output\":[{\"content\":[{\"text\":\"The activation failed because:\\n1. Method name too long (max 30 chars): \\\"responses_two_calls_brace_in_string\\\" \u2014 rename.\\n2. assert_contains / assert_not_contains don't exist in this CL_ABAP_UNIT_ASSERT version \u2014 use assert_equals with contains() or CS checks, e.g. assert_equals( act = boolc( ... CS ... ) exp = abap_true ) or use assert_char_cp. I'll use `assert_equals( act = xsdbool( ... ) exp = abap_true )`.\\n\\nLet me rewrite with method names \u226430 chars: \\n- RESPONSES_BRACE_IN_STRING (25)\\n- CHAT_BRACE_IN_STRING (21)\\n- SPLIT_ENTRIES_BRACE (20)\\n- BALANCED_BRACE_IN_STRING (25)\\n\\nFor contains checks: use `cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals( act = xsdbool( lv_args CS 'status' ) exp = abap_false msg = ... )`.\",\"type\":\"reasoning_text\"}],\"encrypted_content\":null,\"id\":\"rs_202610071954016836542f490949ed\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":[],\"type\":\"reasoning\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"include\\\":\\\"testclasses\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"ZCL_PIA_00_LLM_HTTP\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"CLASS ltcl_parse_calls DEFINITION FINAL FOR TESTING\\\\n  RISK LEVEL HARMLESS DURATION SHORT.\\\\n\\\\n  PRIVATE SECTION.\\\\n    METHODS responses_brace_in_string FOR TESTING RAISING cx_static_check.\\\\n    METHODS chat_brace_in_string      FOR TESTING RAISING cx_static_check.\\\\n    METHODS split_entries_brace       FOR TESTING RAISING cx_static_check.\\\\n    METHODS balanced_brace_in_string  FOR TESTING RAISING cx_static_check.\\\\nENDCLASS.\\\\n\\\\nCLASS ltcl_parse_calls IMPLEMENTATION.\\\\n\\\\n  \\\\\\\" bug: brace counting in split_entries/extract_balanced ignores JSON string\\\\n  \\\\\\\" literals, so a source argument containing lv_open = '{'. swallowed the rest\\\\n  \\\\\\\" of the response: the first call kept trailing JSON (\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"call_id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"c1\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}) and the second call was lost.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD responses_brace_in_string.\\\\n    DATA lv_src1 TYPE string.\\\\n    CONCATENATE\\\\n      `{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ZCL_TEST\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"source\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"CLASS zcl_test. METHOD run. DATA lv_open TYPE string.`\\\\n      ` lv_open = '{'. ENDMETHOD. ENDCLASS.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}`\\\\n      INTO lv_src1.\\\\n    DATA(lv_body) =\\\\n      `{` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      `\\\\\\\"output\\\\\\\":[` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      `{` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      `\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"function_call\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      `\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"fc_1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"call_id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"c1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"write_source\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      `\\\\\\\"arguments\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"` \\u0026\\u0026 lv_src1 \\u0026\\u0026 `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      `\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      `},{` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      `\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"function_call\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      `\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"fc_2\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"call_id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"c2\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"read_object\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      `\\\\\\\"arguments\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ZCL_TEST\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      `\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      `}` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      `]}`.\\\\n\\\\n    DATA(lt_calls) = zcl_pia_00_llm_http=\\u003eparse_calls_responses( lv_body ).\\\\n\\\\n    \\\\\\\" both calls must survive the unbalanced brace inside the first argument\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = 2 act = lines( lt_calls ) msg = 'second call lost' ).\\\\n\\\\n    IF lines( lt_calls ) \\u003e= 1.\\\\n      cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n        act = lt_calls[ 1 ]-id   exp = 'c1' ).\\\\n      cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n        act = lt_calls[ 1 ]-name exp = 'write_source' ).\\\\n      \\\\\\\" the first argument must be exactly the object, no trailing JSON\\\\n      cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n        exp = abap_false\\\\n        act  = xsdbool( lt_calls[ 1 ]-arguments CS 'status' )\\\\n        msg  = |arguments overran: { lt_calls[ 1 ]-arguments }| ).\\\\n      cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n        exp = abap_true\\\\n        act  = xsdbool( lt_calls[ 1 ]-arguments CS `'{'` )\\\\n        msg  = |arguments truncated: { lt_calls[ 1 ]-arguments }| ).\\\\n      cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n        exp = abap_true\\\\n        act  = xsdbool( lt_calls[ 1 ]-arguments CP `{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ZCL_TEST\\\\\\\"*` )\\\\n        msg  = |arguments start wrong: { lt_calls[ 1 ]-arguments }| ).\\\\n    ENDIF.\\\\n\\\\n    IF lines( lt_calls ) \\u003e= 2.\\\\n      cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n        act = lt_calls[ 2 ]-id   exp = 'c2' ).\\\\n      cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n        act = lt_calls[ 2 ]-name exp = 'read_object' ).\\\\n      cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n        act = lt_calls[ 2 ]-arguments exp = `{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ZCL_TEST\\\\\\\"}` ).\\\\n    ENDIF.\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD chat_brace_in_string.\\\\n    DATA lv_src1 TYPE string.\\\\n    CONCATENATE\\\\n      `{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ZCL_TEST\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"source\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"CLASS zcl_test. METHOD run.`\\\\n      ` lv_open = '{'. ENDMETHOD. ENDCLASS.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}`\\\\n      INTO lv_src1.\\\\n    DATA(lv_body) =\\\\n      `{` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      `\\\\\\\"choices\\\\\\\":[{` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      `\\\\\\\"message\\\\\\\":{` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      `\\\\\\\"role\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"assistant\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      `\\\\\\\"tool_calls\\\\\\\":[` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      `{` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      `\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"c1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"function\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      `\\\\\\\"function\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"write_source\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"arguments\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"` \\u0026\\u0026 lv_src1 \\u0026\\u0026 `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      `},{` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      `\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"c2\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"function\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      `\\\\\\\"function\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"read_object\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"arguments\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ZCL_TEST\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      `}` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      `]}}]}`.\\\\n\\\\n    DATA(lt_calls) = zcl_pia_00_llm_http=\\u003eparse_calls_chat( lv_body ).\\\\n\\\\n    cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n      exp = 2 act = lines( lt_calls ) msg = 'second call lost' ).\\\\n\\\\n    IF lines( lt_calls ) \\u003e= 1.\\\\n      cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n        act = lt_calls[ 1 ]-id   exp = 'c1' ).\\\\n      cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n        act = lt_calls[ 1 ]-name exp = 'write_source' ).\\\\n      cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n        exp = abap_false\\\\n        act  = xsdbool( lt_calls[ 1 ]-arguments CS 'function' )\\\\n        msg  = |arguments overran: { lt_calls[ 1 ]-arguments }| ).\\\\n      cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n        exp = abap_true\\\\n        act  = xsdbool( lt_calls[ 1 ]-arguments CS `'{'` )\\\\n        msg  = |arguments truncated: { lt_calls[ 1 ]-arguments }| ).\\\\n    ENDIF.\\\\n\\\\n    IF lines( lt_calls ) \\u003e= 2.\\\\n      cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n        act = lt_calls[ 2 ]-id   exp = 'c2' ).\\\\n      cl_abap_unit_assert=\\u003eassert_equals(\\\\n        act = lt_calls[ 2 ]-arguments exp = `{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ZCL_TEST\\\\\\\"}` ).\\\\n    ENDIF.\\\\n  ENDMETHOD.\\\\n\\\\n  METHOD split_entries_brace.\\\\n    \\\\\\\" array with two objects; a string value in the first holds a lone '{'\\\\n    DATA(lv_arr) =\\\\n      `[` \\u0026\\u0026\\\\n      `{\\\\\\\\\